## 7. System Health Metrics

### ML Lens Observability Pillars
| Pillar | Coverage | Maturity |
|--------|----------|----------|
| Training Observability | Workflow runs, experiment metrics | ✅ Most mature |
| Feature Observability | MLFS feature views — freshness, volume, drift | ⚠️ In progress |
| Data Observability | Any PySpark DataFrame — via ml-dq-sdk | 🔴 Early stage |
| Prediction Observability | Model outputs, serving behavior | 🔴 Mostly planned |

### Alert Detection Logic
- Baselines computed per `metric_key` over configurable reference window (rolling or absolute)
- Detection: compares current value to baseline (mean, std)
- Conditions: single threshold, group (AND logic), complex (N_OF)
- No-data detection supported

**Source**: [ML Observability for Growth Recommendations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6650192184/ML+Observability+for+Growth+Recommendations+Needs+Platform+Capabilities+Gaps+and+Path+Forward), [ML Lens Alerting Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5989280688/ML+Lens+Alerting+Requirements)

