## 3. Python SDK (`atlassian_ml_lens_sdk`)

### 3.1 Core SDK Usage
```python
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.client.ml_lens_client import MlLensClient
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.client.models import MetricsPayload
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.metrics.metrics import send_metrics

# MetricsPayload dataclass
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class MetricsPayload:
    metric_namespace_and_key: str   # e.g., "kyc.reranking.NDCG@1"
    type: str                       # "number", "string", or "boolean"
    value: Any# the measured number
    timestamp: Optional[Union[str, int, float]] = None
    source_type: Optional[str] = None
    tags: Dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)

# Publish metrics
payloads = [
    MetricsPayload(
        metric_namespace_and_key="namespace.evaluation_metric.mean",
        type="number",
        value=1.23,
        tags={"env": "dev"}
    ),
]
send_metrics(run_id="example-run-id", metrics=payloads)
```

### 3.2 Naming Conventions
- `metric_namespace_and_key` is a single dotted string: `<team>.<domain>.<metric_name>`
- After last-dot split by backend: `namespace` column + `metric_key` column
- Must have at least one `.` separator
- Tags carry slice dimensions (tenant_id, region, model_id, etc.)

### 3.3 Read Path (Upcoming/New)
```python
# get_aggregated_metric() wraps GET /api/v1/metrics/aggregated-analysis/{namespace.key}
results = client.get_aggregated_metric(
    metric="metric.namespace.key",
    filter_by='{"tag_name": ["value1"]}',
    resolution_type="FULL_RANGE",
    roll_up="average",
)
```

**Source**: [ML Lens: How it works](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6973026460/ML+Lens+How+it+works), [ML Studio ML Lens Evaluation Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6078891934/ML+Studio+ML+Lens+Evaluation+Metrics)

