## 4. Drift Detection Metrics

### 4.1 Platform-Level Drift (ML Lens Native)
The drift detection job runs every ~5 minutes on StarRocks, computing:

| Metric Namespace | Description | Algorithm |
|-----------------|-------------|-----------|
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_d` | KS D-statistic | max(|CDF_current - CDF_reference|) over100 quantile pairs |
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue` | KS p-value | Statistical significance of distribution difference |
| `feature_observability.drift.psi` | Population Stability Index | Σ (cur_pct − ref_pct) × ln(cur_pct / ref_pct) across bins |

**Configuration**:
- Reference window: sliding (default 28d) or fixed period
- Baseline: user-supplied summary stats or computed from reference window
- Current window: 1 day (default)
- Alert thresholds: KS p-value ≤ 0.05 (drift detected), KS D ≥ 0.1 (significant shift)

### 4.2 Data Quality SDK Drift Metrics (`atlassian_ml_dq_sdk`)
The SDK provides these drift detection classes in `atlassian_ml_dq_sdk.metrics.distribution`:

| Class | Purpose | Parameters | Returns |
|-------|---------|-----------|---------|
| `PopulationStabilityIndex` | Distribution shift via PSI | column, reference_distribution, bins=10 | PSI float |
| `KLDivergence` | KL divergence between distributions | column, reference_distribution, bins=10 | KL value float |
| `KolmogorovSmirnov` | Empirical distribution comparison | column, reference_values | KS statistic float |
| `FeatureDrift` | Mean absolute bin frequency difference | column, reference_distribution, bins=10 | Drift value float |

```python
from atlassian_ml_dq_sdk.metrics.distribution import (
    PopulationStabilityIndex, KLDivergence, KolmogorovSmirnov, FeatureDrift
)

psi = PopulationStabilityIndex("feature_col", reference_distribution, bins=10)
kl = KLDivergence("feature_col", reference_distribution, bins=10)
ks = KolmogorovSmirnov("feature_col", reference_values)
drift = FeatureDrift("feature_col", reference_distribution, bins=10)
```

### 4.3 Cosine Similarity for NLP Embedding Drift
- **Threshold**: cosine < 0.60 indicates drift (per existing Atlassian documentation)
- **Method**: Compute cosine similarity between sample of production embeddings and reference training dataset embeddings
- **Implementation**: Not native to ML Lens SDK — teams compute externally and emit as custom metrics
- **Related**: FP32→INT8 migration analysis shows cosine ~0.919 mean considered "significant drift" requiring reindex; safe zone is ~0.95+

**Source**: [Drift Detection Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6192530763/Drift+Detection+Metrics), [[Design] ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349/Design+ML+Lens+Platform+Data+Drift+Detection), [Model drift identification and mitigation strategies](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CA3/pages/1953707277/Model+drift+identification+and+mitigation+strategies)

