## 3. Per-Endpoint SLO IaC Patterns

### 3.1 What It Is
Encoding Service Level Objectives per API endpoint as Terraform code, registered in Atlassian's **Tome** platform (SLO tracking/monitoring).

### 3.2 Tome Resource Hierarchy

**Source:** [Best practice for TOME & SignalFX with Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~701218d2df3d0880048348a2a3ced7b9eb167/pages/6702725855), [Guide to Creating Tome Capabilities and SLOs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a9191ae51bcc411c9dcbe043d8b219f0/pages/6137977406)

```
Team → Product → Capability → SLO / SLO Group
```

| Resource | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `tome_team` | Organizational owner |
| `tome_product` | Product grouping |
| `tome_capability` | A specific service capability (e.g., "prompt moderation") |
| `tome_slo` | Individual SLO (reliability, latency, performance) |
| `tome_slo_group` | Roll-up SLO across cohorts (region, shard, etc.) |

### 3.3 Tome SLO Terraform Resource

```hcl
resource "tome_capability" "prompt_moderation" {
  name= "Prompt Moderation"
  description = "Content moderation for AI-generated prompts"
  owner       = "responsible-ai-team"
  importance  = 1  # Tier 1
  product     = tome_product.responsible_ai.id
  team        = tome_team.ai_safety.id
}

resource "tome_slo_group" "prompt_mod_reliability" {
  name       = "Prompt Moderation Reliability"
  capability = tome_capability.prompt_moderation.id
  service_id = "responsible-ai-api"
  type       = "RELIABILITY"

  good_query_template = <<-EOT
    A = data('responsible-ai-api.request.count',
      filter=filter('environment_type', 'prod')
      and filter('endpoint', '/v1/moderation/prompt')
      and (not filter('http_status_code_group', '5xx'))
      and $${filter},
      rollup='sum').sum().publish(label='A', enable=True)
  EOT

  bad_query_template = <<-EOT
    B = data('responsible-ai-api.request.count',
      filter=filter('environment_type', 'prod')
      and filter('endpoint', '/v1/moderation/prompt')
      and filter('http_status_code_group', '5xx')
      and $${filter},
      rollup='sum').sum().publish(label='B', enable=True)
  EOT

  objective =99.9
  is_draft= true# Start as draft, commit after stable
  auto_sync = true

  cohort {
    type= "REGION"
    members = "all"
  }
}
```

### 3.4 SLO Types in Tome

| Type | Use Case | Key Fields |
|------|----------|------------|
| `RELIABILITY` | Error rate / success rate | `good_query_template`, `bad_query_template`, `objective` |
| `PERFORMANCE` | Latency percentile | `good_query_template`, `bad_query_template`, `objective`, `performance_target` |
| `UI_PERFORMANCE` | Frontend rendering | `experience_key`, `population`, `performance_target` |

### 3.5 Encoding SLOs as Terraform Locals (Detector Cross-Reference)

**Source:** [STRA-202605-06](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-267) — "Encode the targets as Terraform locals so detectors reference the same source of truth"

```hcl
# operations/terraform/locals.tf
locals {
  slo_targets = {
    prompt_moderation = {
      endpoint= "/v1/moderation/prompt"
      latency_p99_ms  = 6000
      availability= 99.9
      error_budget= 0.001# 1- 0.999}
    image_moderation = {
      endpoint        = "/v1/moderation/image"
      latency_p99_ms  = null# not latency-gated
      availability    = 99.9
      error_budget    = 0.001
    }
    agent_moderation = {
      endpoint        = "/v1/moderation/agent"
      latency_p99_ms  = null
      availability    = 99.9
      error_budget    = 0.001
    }
    output_moderation = {
      endpoint        = "/v1/moderation/output"
      ttfb_ms         = 1500
      availability    = 99.9
      error_budget    = 0.001
    }}
}
```

Then detectors reference these:
```hcl
resource "signalfx_detector" "prompt_mod_p99_escape" {
  name = "[responsible-ai-api] Prompt Moderation P99 > ${local.slo_targets.prompt_moderation.latency_p99_ms}ms"
  # ... uses local.slo_targets.prompt_moderation.latency_p99_ms as threshold
}
```

### 3.6 Configuration-Driven Pattern (Jira Align Example)

For services with many endpoints, use Terraform's `for_each`:

```hcl
variable "endpoint_slos" {
  type = map(object({
    endpoint= string
    slo_objective = number
    slo_type      = string
  }))
  default = {
    prompt_mod = { endpoint = "/v1/moderation/prompt", slo_objective = 99.9, slo_type = "RELIABILITY" }
    image_mod  = { endpoint = "/v1/moderation/image",  slo_objective = 99.9, slo_type = "RELIABILITY" }
  }
}

resource "tome_slo_group" "endpoint_reliability" {
  for_each   = var.endpoint_slos
  name       = "${each.key} Reliability"
  capability = tome_capability.moderation[each.key].id
  service_id = "responsible-ai-api"
  type       = each.value.slo_typeobjective  = each.value.slo_objective
  is_draft   = true
  # ... good_query_template / bad_query_template
}
```

