# Deep Research Report: ML Engineering Skills Domain Knowledge

## 1. ML Training Pipeline — Atlassian's Standard Path

### What it is
Atlassian's standard ML training path (FY25-26) follows: **Databricks + MLflow → ML Studio orchestration → MSP/Tarot v3 registration → Micros/SageMaker/TEAMServe deployment**. [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091/End-to-End+ML+Framework+Atlassian)

### How it works — Architecture Layers
1. **Data Lake & Feature Stores** — Socrates tables, Tecton feature views
2. **Training & Experimentation** — Databricks notebooks, MLflow experiments and runs
3. **Workflow Orchestration (ML Studio)** — Workflows as DAGs of modules (data prep, training, evaluation, packaging, registration)
4. **Model Registry & Serving Control Plane** — MSP / Tarot v3 model registry; ML Registry for lineage; Deployment Store for artifact replication
5. **Serving Backends** — SageMaker endpoints and TEAMServe Triton instances
6. **Product Services (Micros)** — service descriptors (`*.sd.yml`) referencing MSP model groups/versions

### Training Frameworks
- **ML Studio** — Atlassian's workflow orchestration platform; manages workflows, modules, datasets, and integration with Databricks/ML Fabric/MSP. Supports up to 75 nested workflows per parent, 50 nodes per workflow (3,750 nodes total). [ML Studio One Pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3236010671/ML+Studio+One+Pager)
- **Praxis ML** — Atlassian's emerging unified training framework. Provides base classes (Trainer, Evaluator, Deployer), preconfigured Recipes, CLI, and Job Scheduler (Kubernetes/Kueue). Designed for both local and distributed (multi-GPU/TPU) training. [Praxis ML](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120208fca6f07a4e3413ea2ec03c396573bb7/pages/6071324408/Praxis+ML+Atlassian+Unified+Training+Surface)
- **ML Fabric** — Unified compute platform supporting multi-node jobs with EFA (3200Gbps bandwidth, 16× improvement). [Distributed Training Supercharged on ML Fabric](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/11/17/6049073470/Distributed+Training+Supercharged+on+ML+Fabric)

### Continuous Model Training
ML Studio supports automated retraining via triggers at regular intervals. Pipeline steps: data preparation → validation → model training → evaluation → model validation (Launchpad). [ML Studio Supports Continuous Model Training](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2024/12/19/4551130272/ML+Studio+Supports+Continuous+Model+Training)

### How it applies to SKILL.md
The `ml-training-pipeline` SKILL should encode:
- **When-to-use**: When user asks to train/retrain a model, set up continuous training, run HPO, evaluate model performance
- **Tools orchestrated**: ML Studio (workflow creation/execution), MLflow (experiment tracking), Databricks (compute), ML Fabric (distributed GPU), Praxis ML (unified recipes)
- **Workflow steps**: Data prep → Feature engineering → Training (multi-seed, k-fold) → Evaluation → Packaging → Registration

---

## 2. MLE Elevated Standards (§10.2 Reference Patterns)

### What it is
The elevated rigor standards for ML Engineering at Atlassian, requiring statistical robustness beyond typical "train once and ship" patterns.

### How it works — Concrete Checklist

| Standard | Description | Implementation |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| **Multi-seed training** | Run same experiment with≥3 different random seeds to verify result stability | Set `seed=[42, 123, 456, 789, 2024]` in training config; report mean± std of primary metric |
| **Full k-fold cross-validation** | Stratified k-fold (k=5minimum) to validate model generalization | Use `StratifiedKFold` for classification; report per-fold metrics and aggregate |
| **Slice-everything evaluation** | Evaluate model on all meaningful data slices (per-tenant, per-region, per-connector, per-content-type) | Define slice dimensions upfront; fail if any critical slice degrades >X% |
| **HPO to statistical convergence** | Hyperparameter optimization must run until improvement converges (not fixed budget) | Use Bayesian optimization (Optuna/Ray Tune); stop when improvement < ε for N trials |
| **Sensitivity analysis** | Perturb each hyperparameter ±10-20% and measure output stability | Document which parameters the model is sensitive to |
| **Reproducibility** | Any training run must be exactly reproducible from registry artifacts | Log: code hash, data version, config YAML, seed, environment (Docker image hash) |

### How it applies to SKILL.md
Encode as a **pre-submit checklist** in the training skill:
```
## Elevated Standards Checklist (§10.2)
- [ ] Multi-seed:≥3 seeds, mean ± std reported
- [ ] K-fold:≥5 folds, per-fold metrics logged
- [ ] Slice evaluation: all critical slices pass threshold
- [ ] HPO convergence: Bayesian search ran to convergence (Δ< ε for 10 trials)
- [ ] Sensitivity: ±15% perturbation of top-5 HPs documented
- [ ] Reproducibility: code hash + data version + config + seed + Docker image logged in MLflow
```

