```markdown
# ml-training-pipeline SKILL

## When to Use
- User asks to train/retrain a model
- User needs to set up continuous model training
- User wants to run HPO or evaluate model performance
- User needs to validate elevated standards compliance

## Tools Orchestrated
- ML Studio (workflow DAGs, modules, scheduling)
- MLflow (experiment tracking, artifact logging)
- Databricks (compute, notebooks)
- ML Fabric / Praxis ML (distributed training, recipes)
- Tecton/MLFS (feature retrieval for training data)
- Tarot v3 / ML Registry (model registration, lineage)

## Workflow Steps

### Step 1: Data Preparation
- Fetch training data from Socrates/feature store
- Run Feature DQ audit (SOP-2step 4)
- Validate schema, check coverage/freshness/sparsity

### Step 2: Training Configuration
- Define experiment in MLflow
- Set multi-seed config (≥3 seeds)
- Configure k-fold (≥5 stratified folds)
- Set HPO search space with convergence criteria

### Step 3: Parallel Training Variants
- Launch multi-seed runs in parallel
- Each seed runs full k-fold
- Log per-fold metrics to MLflow
- HPO: Bayesian optimization until convergence (Δ < ε for 10 trials)

### Step 4: Evaluation (Slice-Everything)
- Evaluate on all critical slices (connector × region × tenant)
- Compare to baseline model
- Run sensitivity analysis (±15% on top-5 HPs)
- Gate: all slices must pass threshold

### Step 5: Elevated Standards Checklist (§10.2)
- [ ] Multi-seed: ≥3 seeds, mean ± std reported
- [ ] K-fold: ≥5 folds, per-fold metrics logged
- [ ] Slice evaluation: all critical slices pass
- [ ] HPO convergence: confirmed
- [ ] Sensitivity: documented
- [ ] Reproducibility: code hash + data version + config + seed + Docker image

### Step 6: Packaging & Registration
- Package model artifacts (tar.gz)
- Upload to Tarot v3
- Register component version with full metadata and lineage
- Compliance: ensure compliant build pipeline

## Human Confirmation Required
- Before deploying to production (Step 6→ deployment skill)
- When any elevated standard check fails
- When HPO suggests significant architecture change

## Anti-Patterns
- Single-seed training → use multi-seed
- Fixed HPO budget → use convergence-based stopping
- Skipping slice evaluation → evaluate all slices
- Training without feature DQ check → always run SOP-2 first
- Manual artifact tracking → always use MLflow + Tarot v3 lineage
```

