## 2. MLE Elevated Standards (§10.2 Reference Patterns)

### What it is
The elevated rigor standards for ML Engineering at Atlassian, requiring statistical robustness beyond typical "train once and ship" patterns.

### How it works — Concrete Checklist

| Standard | Description | Implementation |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| **Multi-seed training** | Run same experiment with≥3 different random seeds to verify result stability | Set `seed=[42, 123, 456, 789, 2024]` in training config; report mean± std of primary metric |
| **Full k-fold cross-validation** | Stratified k-fold (k=5minimum) to validate model generalization | Use `StratifiedKFold` for classification; report per-fold metrics and aggregate |
| **Slice-everything evaluation** | Evaluate model on all meaningful data slices (per-tenant, per-region, per-connector, per-content-type) | Define slice dimensions upfront; fail if any critical slice degrades >X% |
| **HPO to statistical convergence** | Hyperparameter optimization must run until improvement converges (not fixed budget) | Use Bayesian optimization (Optuna/Ray Tune); stop when improvement < ε for N trials |
| **Sensitivity analysis** | Perturb each hyperparameter ±10-20% and measure output stability | Document which parameters the model is sensitive to |
| **Reproducibility** | Any training run must be exactly reproducible from registry artifacts | Log: code hash, data version, config YAML, seed, environment (Docker image hash) |

### How it applies to SKILL.md
Encode as a **pre-submit checklist** in the training skill:
```
## Elevated Standards Checklist (§10.2)
- [ ] Multi-seed:≥3 seeds, mean ± std reported
- [ ] K-fold:≥5 folds, per-fold metrics logged
- [ ] Slice evaluation: all critical slices pass threshold
- [ ] HPO convergence: Bayesian search ran to convergence (Δ< ε for 10 trials)
- [ ] Sensitivity: ±15% perturbation of top-5 HPs documented
- [ ] Reproducibility: code hash + data version + config + seed + Docker image logged in MLflow
```

