## 6. Responsible-AI-API Production Patterns (§5.3)

### 6.1 Two-Stage Moderation

**Architecture:**
```
Client → responsible-ai-api → Stage 1 (Gemma4fast classifier, ~200ms)
                              ↓ (2% escalated - DISALLOW from Stage 1)
                              Stage 2 (GPT-OSS 20B fine-tuned, detailed reasoning)
                              ↓ DISALLOW confirmed OR Overturn (false positive)
```

**Key metrics:**
- `rai.cascade.stage1.latency_ms` — P50≤ 150ms, P95 < 300ms
- `rai.cascade.stage1.blocking_rate` — target ~2%
- `rai.cascade.e2e.blocking_rate` — target <0.35%
- `rai.cascade.stage2.overturn_rate` — % overturned
- `rai.cascade.stage2.precision` — target >95%

**Feature gates:**
| Gate | Type | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| `rai_api_enable_cascade_moderation` | rollout | Master switch, % per tenant |
| `rai_api_cascade_stage1_variant` | config | Selects Gemma 4 variant (1b/2b/4b) |
| `rai_api_cascade_skip_stage2` | kill-switch | Emergency: skip Stage 2, use Stage 1 directly |

[Two-Stage Prompt Moderator — Architecture Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/7064183361/Two-Stage+Prompt+Moderator+Architecture+Design)

### 6.2 Fail-Open Kill-Switch

**Pattern:** When model inference fails (timeout, circuit breaker open, parse error), return `ALLOWED` instead of blocking the user.

**Feature flags in production:**
- `rai_api_should_fail_open_when_model_timesout` — fail-open on model timeout
- `rai_api_enable_fail_open_on_circuit_breaker_open` — fail-open when circuit breaker opens

**Circuit breaker config:** `fail_max=30` (Triton circuit breaker)

**Observable metric:** `fail_open_count` with `reason` tag (timeout / circuit_breaker / parse_error)

[responsible-ai-api](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TRUST/pages/5927717332/responsible-ai-api)

### 6.3 Per-Tenant Token Bucket Rate Limiter

**Problem:** Single noisy tenant triggered SageMaker worker exhaustion (8,251 errors/min);99.6% of errors from one tenant.

**Implementation:**
- In-process token bucket keyed on `tenant_id`
- No external state needed (single-tenant burst is threat model)
- Hook from image controller's `before_request`
- HTTP 429 with `Retry-After` header on limit exceeded
- Default capacity sized for legitimate large-batch tenants
- Dynamic config for tuning without redeploy

**Configuration pattern (from Burst Rate Limiting):**
```
bucketKey = (tenantId, normalizedApiPath, httpMethod)
Parameters:
  - capacity (bucket size): max tokens
  - refill_rate: tokens per second
  - refill_period_ms: 1000
```

**Design principles:**
1. Fail-open on error (config missing, Redis unavailable)
2. Per-tenant isolation
3. Dynamic config via Statsig (no code changes)
4. Ship behind default-off gate → ramp gradually

[OPP-202605-03Per-tenant rate limiting](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-263)
[Per-Tenant Rate Limiting Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120205e3887bb099b4a43935b969e110bdf55/pages/6296999849/Per-Tenant+Rate+Limiting+Strategy)

### 6.4 Canary Auto-Rollback

**Pattern from responsible-ai-api incident PIR:**
- Production rollback via `atlas micros rollback` completed in ~3 minutes
- Pollinator coverage (post-deployment verification) added to catch schema breaks before promotion to100%
- Spinnaker canary analysis compares canary vs baseline stack on 5xx rate, error rate thresholds
- Automatic rollback triggers if canary metrics exceed threshold

[PIR-301052- responsible-ai-api breaking schema change](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/inckb/pages/6897024494/PIR-301052+-+HOT-301624+-+Sev2+-+Rovo+Agent+scenario+create+reliability+dropped+to+0+due+to+breaking+schema+change+in+responsible-ai-api)

### Deployment Safety Checklist (for SKILL.md)
```
## responsible-ai-api Production Pattern Checklist
- [ ] Two-stage moderation: Stage 1 fast classifier + Stage 2 detailed (escalation only)
- [ ] Fail-open kill-switch: All inference failures return ALLOWED (with metric)
- [ ] Circuit breaker: fail_max configured, fail-open on CB open
- [ ] Per-tenant token bucket: keyed on tenant_id, dynamic config, default-off gate
- [ ] Feature gates: master rollout switch + kill-switch per stage
- [ ] Canary deployment: Spinnaker progressive rollout (10% → 50% → 100%)
- [ ] Pollinator checks: post-deploy verification payload validates all endpoints
- [ ] Rollback target: < 10min rollback (actual: ~3 min via atlas micros rollback)
- [ ] Metrics: stage, decision, model, latency, blocking_rate, overturn_rate, fail_open_count
```

