## 10. Anti-Patterns (for SKILL.md)

Based on incidents and patterns observed:

| Anti-Pattern | Why it's bad | What to do instead |
|---|---|---|
| Train once with single seed | Results may be noise, not signal | Multi-seed (≥3), report mean ± std |
| Skip slice evaluation | Model may fail on minority segments | Evaluate on all meaningful slices |
| Deploy without kill-switch | Cannot revert without redeploy | Always have independent runtime switch |
| Couple healthcheck to sidecar | Sidecar startup race causes AZ-wide failures | Decouple /healthcheck from sidecar readiness |
| No per-tenant rate limit | Single tenant can exhaust shared resources | Token bucket keyed on tenant_id |
| Rely on deployment rollback only | Rollback is slow and may fail | Fail-open + feature flag + auto-rollback |
| Single model for all traffic | No graceful degradation | Two-stage: fast classifier + detailed (escalation only) |
| Register model without lineage | Cannot reproduce or audit | Use Tarot v3 with full lineage capture |
| Skip Launchpad validation | Discover packaging issues in production | Always validate on Launchpad before prod deployment |
| Fixed HPO budget | May stop before convergence or waste compute | Bayesian optimization with convergence stopping |

