## 5. SLO Infrastructure-as-Code (Tome)

### What It Is
Tome is Atlassian's internal platform — the **source of truth for Capability SLOs**. It tracks reliability and performance objectives, integrates with SignalFx for alerting, and drives quarterly review cadences.

### How It Works

**Key Concepts:**
- **Capability:** An end-to-end user experience (e.g., "A user can view an issue")
- **SLO:** Measurable reliability/performance goal (e.g., 99.9% over 28-day rolling window)
- **SLI:** The actual metric being measured
- **Error Budget:** `(SLI - SLO) / (1 - SLO)` — how much room before breach
- **Burn Rate:** Error Rate / Error Budget — how fast budget is consumed

**Per-Endpoint SLOs for responsible-ai-api (fromSTRA-202605-07):**
| Endpoint | SLO Target |
|----------|------------|
| prompt | p99≤ 6s |
| agent | p99 ≤ 8s |
| image | p99 ≤ 10s |
| output first-token | ≤ 2s |
| 5xx rate | ≤ 0.1% |
| fail-open rate | ≤ 0.5% |

**Terraform SLO Resource:**
```hcl
resource "tome_slo" "prompt_reliability" {
  name       = "prompt moderation reliability"
  capability = tome_capability.responsible_ai.id
  type       = "RELIABILITY"
  objective  = 99.9
  good_query = "data('http.response.count', filter=...5xx excluded...)"
  bad_query  = "data('http.response.count', filter=...5xx only...)"
  pollinator_uuids = ["uuid-of-synthetic-check"]
}

resource "tome_slo_group" "per_region" {
  name = "responsible-ai-api per-region"
  capability = tome_capability.responsible_ai.id
  slo_group_type = "REGION"
  cohort {
    type = "REGION"
    objective = 99.95
    good_query_template = "data('metric', filter=$${filter})..."
  }
  cohort {
    type = "GLOBAL"
    objective = 99.9}
}
```

**Alert Types from Tome:**
- Gradual burn (early warning)
- Moderate burn
- Steep burn (rapid consumption)
- Breach (SLO violated)

**Registration Process (from STRA-202605-07):**
1. Cross-team alignment on threshold values
2. Register with the SLO API (via Tome Terraform provider)
3. Wire into Sauron and a quarterly review cadence

### How It Applies to Skills/Tools

**Part of `signalfx_detector_iac` tool** (SLO dimension):
- Generate `tome_slo` / `tome_slo_group` Terraform resources
- Define good_query/bad_query in SignalFlow
- Configure alert recipients and severity
- Link to Pollinator synthetic checks

**Source:** [Guide to SLOs and Tome](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agents/pages/5574209974), [STRA-202605-07](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-256), [SLO Groups Implementation Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121ac1c28b3d640400ea4e4e655ba8b334a/pages/7037249779), [Tome - overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~701215303a9cfa6744565be65e74325bf3776/pages/3622005259)

