## 4. Incident Response — JSM Ops REST API & PIR Drafting

### What It Is
JSM (Jira Service Management) provides the incident management lifecycle through its Incident API. At Atlassian, incidents are tracked via HOT tickets and post-incident reviews (PIRs).

### How It Works — JSM Incident API

**API Endpoints (from JSM Incident API documentation):**
```
POST /incident    — Create incident
GET /incident/{issueID}           — Get incident details
POST /incident/{issueID}/major— Set major incident status
DELETE /incident/{issueID}        — Delete incident

Alert Management:
POST /incident/{issueID}/alerts   — Link alerts to incident
DELETE /incident/{issueID}/alerts— Unlink alerts

Responders/Stakeholders:
POST /incident/{issueID}/responders
POST /incident/{issueID}/stakeholders
```

**Tech Stack:** Kotlin, Spring Boot, DynamoDB, SQS
**Key Capabilities:** Create/read/delete incidents, manage responders/stakeholders, associate OpsGenie alerts (async), Slack integration via OpsGenie Chat, PIR creation and linking, major incident status.

**PIR Process (from Post-Incident Reviews documentation):**
- **Triggers:** Mandatory for Sev 0/1/2; optional for Sev 3
- **OLA:** 10business days from incident resolution to PIR approval (role doc says<5BD)
- **PIR Content:** Timeline with timestamps, impact assessment, root cause (5Whys), action items with owners/deadlines, lessons learned
- **PIR Types:** Full PIR (Sev 0-2), Express PIR/PIRX (Sev 2-3), Public PIR/PPIR (customer-facing)

**Key Metrics (from PIR Actions Guidance):**
- **TTD< 15 minutes** (Time to Detect - Impact Detection Time minus Impact Start Time)
- **TTR < 2 hours** (Time to Resolve - Impact End Time minus Impact Start Time)  
- **TTH < 25 minutes** (HOT creation from major severity breach)
- **TTC < 30 minutes** (Time to Communicate from HOT creation)

### Incident SOP (Role Doc §6SOP-3)

**SOP-3 Incident Response Protocol:**
- TTD < 15m target
- TTR < 2h target
- **30-minute status cadence** (regular structured updates in incident channel)
- Severity classification (cross-correlation of signals)
- Escalation procedures
- PIR < 5 business days

**Severity Classification Matrix:**
| Severity | Impact | PIR Required | PPIR |
|----------|--------|--------------|------|
| Sev 0 | Crisis | Mandatory✅ (+ELT review) | Mandatory |
| Sev 1 | Critical | Mandatory ✅ | Often mandatory |
| Sev 2 | Major | Mandatory ✅ | Optional |
| Sev 3 | Minor | Optional | N/A |

### How It Applies to Skills/Tools

**`incident_pir_drafter` tool** should support:
- Auto-generate PIR skeleton from incident timeline (Slack messages, HOT ticket data)
- Populate standard sections: Timeline, Impact, Root Cause, Action Items, Lessons
- Calculate TTD/TTR/TTH/TTC metrics
- Cross-reference similar past incidents
- Create PIR ticket in OpsJ and linked Confluence doc

**`ml-incident-response` skill** should orchestrate:
1. Detect incident signals (SLO burn, alert fire, CB trip)
2. Classify severity using cross-correlation
3. Create JSM incident (auto or confirm based on severity)
4. Establish30-minute status cadence in Slack
5. Execute runbook steps
6. Generate PIR draft on resolution
7. Track action items to completion

**Autonomy tier mapping:**
- 🟢 Autonomous: Detect, triage, run diagnostics, post status updates, draft PIR
- 🟡 Confirm: Declare incident (Sev 2-3), execute standard runbook steps
- 🔴 Escalate: Declare Sev 0-1, rollback decisions, customer communications

**Source:** [JSM Incident API — Comprehensive Flow Documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121b83dce7f21514aa79fbbbb2b1ec609f7/pages/6899447939), [Post-Incident Reviews (PIRs)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020569da089a21d46c89d014c3c8a40039d/pages/6272935146), [Google SRE Book Summary](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/6798517849)

