## 8. Google SRE Incident Management Practices

### Key Patterns (from Google SRE Book Summary — internal Atlassian analysis)

**Incident Command System (ICS):**
| Role | Responsibility | AI SRE Analogue |
|------|---------------|-----------------|
| Incident Commander (IC) | Coordinates response, assigns tasks | Human on-call engineer |
| Operations Lead | Investigates and diagnoses | **AI SRE agent** |
| Communications Lead | Manages stakeholder updates | Future extension |

**Postmortem Best Practices:**
- Blameless (systems, not people)
- Collaborative (written live)
- Shared broadly (organizational learning)
- Contains: Timeline + Impact + Root Cause (5 Whys) + Action Items + Lessons

**AI SRE Agent Role (Operations Lead):**
- Gather signals, test hypotheses, feed structured findings to IC
- Updates follow ICS discipline: structured, confident, minimal noise
- Auto-draft postmortem skeleton from investigation log
- Never attribute to individuals (always blameless)

**SRE Agent Onboarding Phases (from Agentic Operations):**
1. **Initiation:** Core SRE skills + platform context, no service-specific knowledge
2. **Assignment:** Begins training specific to assigned service
3. **Specialization:** Becomes expert on service failure modes, traffic patterns, deployment history

**Source:** [Google SRE Book — Summary & AI SRE Agent Design Implications](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/6798517849)

