## 6. MLE Elevated Standards — Rigor Patterns

**Source**: Digital MLE Vision (implicit from offline evaluation requirements), [MLE Agent Capability Evaluation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/6983354773), industry-standard ML experiment rigor (NIST AI RMF 1.0, Google ML Best Practices)

### 6.1 Multi-Seed Reproducibility Protocol

```yaml
training_config:
  seeds: [42, 123, 456, 789, 1024]  # Minimum 3, recommended 5
  report_format:
    metric: "mean± std across seeds"
    convergence_check: "std < 0.01 * mean"
  fail_condition: "std > 0.05 * mean → flag instability"
```

### 6.2 Full K-Fold Cross-Validation

```yaml
evaluation_config:
  cv_strategy: "stratified_k_fold"
  k: 5  # Minimum; 10 for smaller datasets
  holdout: true# Always maintain a separate test set
  report:
    per_fold_metrics: true
    aggregate: "mean ± std"
    worst_fold_analysis: true
```

### 6.3 Slice-Everything Evaluation

Mandatory slicing dimensions for any model evaluation:
```yaml
slice_dimensions:
  - connector_type: [full_connector, smart_link, gdrive, sharepoint, byod]
  - region: [us-east-1, eu-central-1, ap-southeast-2, us-west-2]
  - tenant_cohort: [hello, non-hello, enterprise, free]
  - query_type: [navigational, informational, transactional]- content_age: [<7d, 7-30d, 30-90d, >90d]
```

### 6.4 HPO to Statistical Convergence

```python
# Bayesian HPO with convergence detection
convergence_config = {
    "n_initial_points": 10,  # Random exploration
    "max_iterations": 200,
    "convergence_criterion": {
        "window": 20,  # Last 20 trials
        "improvement_threshold": 0.001,  # <0.1% improvement
        "patience": 3# 3 consecutive windows with no improvement
    },
    "optimizer": "gaussian_process",
    "acquisition_function": "expected_improvement"
}
```

### 6.5 Sensitivity Analysis

```yaml
sensitivity_config:
  perturbation_types:
    - feature_dropout: [0.05, 0.10, 0.20]# Drop 5/10/20% of features
    - noise_injection: [0.01, 0.05, 0.10]  # Gaussian noise σ
    - temporal_shift: [1d, 3d, 7d]          # Shift evaluation window- tenant_removal: [1, 5, 10]            # Remove N top tenants
  report:
    metric_delta_per_perturbation: true
    critical_features: "top 10 by impact"
    robustness_score: "min(metric) / baseline(metric)"
```

