# Research Findings: ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook — Scoping `circuit_breaker_control` Tool

## 1. Core Circuit Breaker Configuration (responsible-ai-api + ML-Engine)

### What it is
The ML-Engine Circuit Breaker is a Resilience4j-based TIME_BASED circuit breaker protecting the responsible-ai-api service from cascading failures when ML-Engine or downstream dependencies (AI Gateway, Triton/gRPC, SageMaker) become unhealthy.

### How it works — Configuration Parameters

| Parameter | Value | Purpose |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| `slidingWindowType` | `TIME_BASED` | Evaluates over a time window (not call count) |
| `slidingWindowSize` | `60seconds` | Rolling window duration |
| `minimumNumberOfCalls` | `20` | Minimum calls in window before evaluation |
| `failureRateThreshold` | `20%` | CB opens if failure rate ≥ 20% (aggressive — most Atlassian services use 50%) |
| `waitDurationInOpenState` | `30s` base | Exponential backoff with2.0multiplier, max 60s |
| `permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState` | `20` | Trial probes during half-open |
| `automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled` | `true` | Auto-recovery without manual intervention |
| `exponentialBackoffMultiplier` | `2.0` | Doubles wait on repeated trips |
| `maxWaitDurationInOpenState` | `60s` | Ceiling on exponential backoff |
| `recordFailurePredicate` | `ServerErrorOnlyPredicate` | Only5xx counts as failure |

### How it applies to `circuit_breaker_control`
The tool must understand and be able to **read**, **adjust**, and **override** these parameters. Key operations:
- `get_cb_state` — Return current state (CLOSED/OPEN/HALF_OPEN), buffered calls, failure rate
- `get_cb_config` — Return current parameter values
- `set_cb_threshold` — Modify failureRateThreshold or minimumNumberOfCalls (requires approval gate)
- `force_cb_state` — Transition to OPEN/CLOSED/DISABLED (emergency only)
- `reset_cb` — Clear the sliding window and return to CLOSED

### Source
