## 2. Fail-Open Kill-Switch Pattern (responsible-ai-api)

### What it is
The responsible-ai-api service is **structurally fail-open** — when upstream inference services (AI Gateway, Triton, SageMaker) are unavailable, it returns `ALLOWED` with reduced confidence rather than blocking callers. This is controlled via Switcheroo feature gates.

### How it works
Two distinct kill-switch functions exist in the codebase (`src/inference_models/error_handling.py`):

1. **`should_fail_open_on_model_timeout()`** — Returns ALLOWED when model inference times out (e.g., gRPC deadline exceeded)
2. **`should_fail_open_if_circuit_breaker_open()`** — Returns ALLOWED when CB is in OPEN state

**Current state of endpoint coverage:**
| Endpoint | Fail-Open | Circuit Breaker | Notes |
|----------|-----------|-----------------|-------|
| `/v1/moderation/prompt` | ✅ (centralised) | ✅ | Uses `inference_error_handler()` context manager |
| `/v1/moderation/output` | ✅ (centralised) | ✅ | Uses `inference_error_handler()` context manager |
| `/v1/moderation/agent` | ❌ → ✅ (AI-206) | ❌ → ✅ | Being added per HOT-302120 (May 2026) |
| `/v1/moderation/image` | Partial | Partial | SageMaker-specific handling |

**Kill-switch behaviour:**
- Gate defaults to **OFF** (fail-closed = safe default)
- When gate is ON: timeouts/5xx → return ALLOWED + emit metric `agent_moderation_fail_open` tagged with `reason`
- 4xx errors are **never** fail-opened (client errors pass through)
- Metric tags: `timeout`, `circuit_breaker`, `gateway_error`, `grpc_deadline_exceeded`, `grpc_unavailable`, `aigw_400`, `sagemaker_503`

### How it applies to `circuit_breaker_control`
The tool must expose:
- `toggle_fail_open(endpoint, enabled)` — Enable/disable fail-open for a specific endpoint via Switcheroo
- `get_fail_open_status()` — Check current fail-open gate status for all endpoints
- `get_fail_open_metrics(time_range)` — Query the `fail_open.count` metric with reason breakdown

**Autonomy considerations:** Toggling fail-open is a **🟡 Yellow** operation (human confirmation required before executing, but AI can draft the action).

### Source
- [AI-206: Add fail-open / circuit breaker to agent moderation](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-206)
- [AI-253: Add fail-open observability](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-253)
- [AI-248: responsible-ai-api Optimization Epic](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-248)
- Code path: `src/inference_models/error_handling.py`, `src/feature_service.py`

