## 1. Tecton/MLFS Feature Lifecycle: Generated → Written → Hydrated → Logged → Joined-with-Labels

### What It Is
The feature lifecycle at Atlassian follows a 5-stage pipeline, explicitly documented in [RFC-155: RankerV2 design, Feature Store & Feature logging pipelines](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/5939607897/RFC-155+RankerV2+design+Feature+Store+Feature+logging+pipelines.):

1. **Generated** — Feature is computed in a feature generation data pipeline (Spark/Databricks batch job or Flink stream job)
2. **Written** — Feature values are persisted to the Feature Store (Tecton online/offline store, or MLFS ERS/Delta Lake)
3. **Hydrated** — At inference time, the feature is read from the store and injected into the serving request (the "feature hydration" step)
4. **Logged** — During inference, observed feature values + model scores + request IDs are written to UGC-safe storage for downstream training
5. **Joined-with-Labels** — Logged features are joined with user-interaction signals (e.g., clicks, dwell time) on the request/session ID to construct the training dataset

### How It Works — Concrete Steps

| Stage | System | Key API/Action | Output |
|-------|--------|---------------|--------|
| Generated | Databricks/ML Studio + Spark SQL | `fv.run_transformation(start_time, end_time)` | Spark DataFrame with feature columns |
| Written | Tecton Custom Sink / MLFS egress module | `write_to_online_store()` + `write_to_offline_store()` | Features in DynamoDB/ERS (online) + S3/Delta Lake (offline) |
| Hydrated | Serving pipeline (Kotlin/Python) | `feature_service.get_features(entity_keys)` | Feature vector added to inference request |
| Logged | Feature Logging Pipeline | Write to Plato/TDP OS with `search_request_id` | Feature log table (UGC-safe) |
| Joined-with-Labels | Databricks training pipeline | `JOIN features ON request_id = interactions.request_id` | Training dataset (features + labels) |

### How It Applies to the Skill
The SKILL.md should encode this lifecycle as the canonical mental model. Each operation the AI employee performs maps to one or more stages. The skill should include:
- A lifecycle state diagram that the AI references when diagnosing issues
- Validation checks at each transition point
- Common failure modes per stage (e.g., "Written but not Hydrated" = stale online store; "Logged but not Joined" = missing interaction data)

### Source
- [RFC-155 RankerV2 Feature Lifecycle](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/5939607897/RFC-155+RankerV2+design+Feature+Store+Feature+logging+pipelines.)
- [Live Doc on Ranking Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/6242731920/Live+Doc+on+Ranking+Architecture)
- [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/Digital+MLE+AI+Employee+Vision)

