## 4. Feature Versioning and Registry

### What It Is
Atlassian is building a **Unified Feature Catalog** as the single source of truth for all feature definitions and metadata across Tecton and MLFS. This is the governance backbone for feature versioning.

### Key Components

**MLFS Feature Registry API** (from [RFC: MLFS Feature Registry API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5551830112/RFC+MLFS+Feature+Registry+API)):
- **Control Plane APIs**: Feature Service CRUD, Feature View CRUD, registry management
- **Data Plane APIs**: Online serving, batch retrieval, offline queries

**Unified Feature Catalog Structure** (from [FY26H2 DTI-Ecosystem Unified Feature Catalog: System Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6202634504/)):
- Feature registration via YAML in `unified-feature-catalog` repo
- Metadata sync via scheduled CCE job (every 6 hours)
- Feature discovery API, DataFrame loading, versioning with point-in-time lookup
- SDK module: `load_project_features(project)` → Tecton/MLFS offline store → DataFrame

**Feature YAML Schema** (from [FY26Q3 Feature Quality Check Implementation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6494429824/)):
Required fields per feature definition:
- `name`, `type`, `owner`, `category`, `description`
- `readiness` (not_ready / experimental / ready_for_prod)
- `quality_status` (PASS / WARNING / ERROR)
- `null_rate`, `sparsity_score`
- `deprecation_candidate` (bool + reason)

### How It Applies to the Skill
The skill should encode:
- Feature registration workflow (YAML creation → PR → validation → merge → sync)
- Version comparison operations (old vs new feature view)
- Deprecation candidate identification (automated based on sparsity + importance + cost)
- SDK usage patterns for feature retrieval at training time

