## 6. Digital MLE Autonomy Model for Feature Store Operations

### What It Is
The [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/) defines explicit autonomy levels for feature store operations:

### Autonomy Levels

| Operation | Autonomy | AI Employee Action | Human Role |
|-----------|----------|-------------------|------------|
| Data freshness monitoring against refresh policy | 🟢 Autonomous | Run freshness checks, alert on SLA breach | Sets refresh policy |
| Feature coverage reporting by connector type and region | 🟢 Autonomous | Execute coverage queries, generate reports | Reviews anomalies |
| Training/serving skew detection | 🟢 Autonomous | Run comparison pipelines, flag deviations | Investigates root cause |
| Tenant list refresh | 🟢 Autonomous | Update tenant lists per schedule | Approves cross-team data agreements |
| New data source ingestion | 🟡 Confirm | Propose configuration, prepare PR | Approves and merges |
| Feature deprecation | 🟡 Confirm | Identify candidates, prepare analysis | Makes final decision |
| Cross-team data agreements | 🔴 Human | Surface requirements, draft proposals | Owns relationship |

### How It Applies to the Skill
The SKILL.md should use these autonomy levels as **decision gates**:
- 🟢 Operations execute immediately without waiting for human input
- 🟡 Operations prepare artifacts (PRs, reports, proposals) and pause for confirmation
- 🔴 Operations are flagged for human ownership with context summaries

### Source
- [Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727/)

