## 7. Proposed SKILL.md Outline: `feature-store-operations`

Based on all research, here is the recommended structure:

```markdown
# Feature Store Operations

## Overview
This skill enables autonomous feature store management across Tecton and MLFS, 
covering the full feature lifecycle, data quality auditing, train-serve consistency, 
and feature versioning/registration.

## Prerequisites
- Access to Tecton workspace (prod-filtered) and MLFS registry
- Databricks/ML Studio credentials for DQ pipeline execution
- Read access to coreml_feature_quality_profiles and fact_dq_unified_feature_store_metrics

## Workflow1: Feature Lifecycle Monitoring
[Generated → Written → Hydrated → Logged → Joined-with-Labels validation]

## Workflow 2: Data Quality Audit (SOP-2Step 4)
[Coverage/Freshness/Sparsity × Connector × Region × Tenant]
- Canonical query templates
- Threshold interpretation
- Escalation rules

## Workflow 3: Train-Serve Consistency Check
[Online vs Offline comparison, schema parity, value parity, freshness delta]

## Workflow 4: Feature Registration & Versioning
[YAML creation → Validation → Plan → Apply → Monitor]

## Workflow 5: Feature Deprecation Identification
[Sparsity + Importance + Cost → deprecation_candidate tagging]

## Autonomy Model
[Green/Yellow/Red decision gates per operation type]
```

