## 4. Google SRE Incident Management Practices (Relevant Patterns)

### 4.1 Incident Command System (ICS)

**Roles**:
- **Incident Commander (IC)**: Coordinates response, owns communication
- **Operations Lead**: Investigates and diagnoses (AI SRE agent fits here)
- **Communications Lead**: Manages stakeholder updates

**Key Principles**:
- Declare incidents early — less costly than declaring too late
- Explicit, documented, announced handoffs
- Regular structured updates in incident channel
- No side conversations outside the incident channel

### 4.2 Postmortem Best Practices (Google SRE Book Ch15)

A good postmortem contains:
- **Timeline** with exact timestamps
- **Impact assessment** — who, how long, what was lost
- **Root cause analysis** — 5 Whys past the proximate cause
- **Action items** with owners and deadlines
- **Lessons learned** — systemic changes

**Blameless**: Systems, not people. Collaborative (written live). Shared broadly.

> "An unreviewed postmortem might as well never have existed."

**How it applies**: The AI agent fits as the **Operations Lead** — gathering signals, structuring findings, auto-drafting the postmortem skeleton. Must always be blameless — never attribute to individuals.

**Source**: [Google SRE Book — Summary & AI SRE Agent Design Implications](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/6798517849)

