| `post_status_update` | Slack `chat.postMessage` (threaded) | 🟡 Auto with template |
| `schedule_cadence_reminder` | Internal timer + Slack nudge | 🟡 Auto after T+30m |
| `create_pir_page` | Confluence `POST /wiki/api/v2/pages` | 🟡 Human confirms |
| `update_pir_page` | Confluence `PUT /wiki/api/v2/pages/{id}` | 🟡 Human confirms |
| `link_pir_to_incident` | Jira `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/{key}` (custom field) | 🟡 Human confirms |
| `calculate_metrics` | Derived (TTD/TTR/TTC from timestamps) | 🟢 Autonomous |
| `classify_severity` | Read from incident field | 🟢 Autonomous |
| `extract_timeline_from_slack` | Slack `conversations.replies` + NLP | 🟢 Autonomous |

### 5.2 Data Flow for PIR Generation

```
Incident Resolution Event│
        ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 1. Read Incident     │  JSM API: severity, responders, services,
│    (JSM/Jira)│  timeline, comments, linked alerts
└────────┬─────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 2. Read Slack Thread │  conversations.replies: all messages
│    (Slack API)       │  in incident channel thread
└────────┬─────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 3. Calculate Metrics │  TTD = detection_ts - impact_start_ts
│                      │  TTR = resolution_ts - impact_start_ts
│                      │  TTC = first_comms_ts - incident_ts
└────────┬─────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 4. Generate PIR Body │  Fill template with data:
│    (Storage Format)  │  Summary, Timeline, Impact, Detection,
│                      │  Response, Recovery, Metrics, Actions
└────────┬─────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 5. Create Confluence │  POST /wiki/api/v2/pages
│    Page│  Link to PIR ticket
└────────┬─────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌──────────────────────┐
│ 6. Update Jira       │  Set "Document PIR" field
│    (Link PIR)        │  Comment with link
└──────────────────────┘
```

### 5.3 Existing Workspace Tools to Reuse

Based on the research, these existing MCP tools can be reused:
- **`mcp__atlassian__`**: Jira issue read/update, Confluence page create/update
- **`mcp__slack__`**: `chat.postMessage`, `conversations.replies`, `conversations.history`
- **`mcp__bitbucket__`**: Not directly needed for PIR but used for deployment correlation

**Gaps requiring new tool operations**:
- JSM Incident-specific API calls (`/jsm/incidents/...` for responders, stakeholders, linked alerts)
- Cadence timer/scheduler (30-min reminder loop)
- PIR template rendering engine (transforms structured data → Confluence storage format)
- TTD/TTR/TTC calculation logic
- Slack thread → PIR timeline NLP extraction

### 5.4 Human Confirmation Boundaries

| Action | Autonomy Level | Rationale |
|--------|---------------|-----------|
| Read incident data | 🟢 Fully autonomous | Read-only, no side effects |
| Read Slack thread | 🟢 Fully autonomous | Read-only |
| Post 30-min status update | 🟡 Template + auto | Uses pre-approved template; visible to humans |
| Create PIR page | 🟡 Draft + confirm | AI drafts, human reviews before "publish" |
| Update PIR with new data | 🟡 Draft + confirm | Same — present diff, human approves |
| Transition incident status | 🔴 Human only | Status changes have SLA implications |
| Change severity | 🔴 Human only | Severity changes trigger different paging |
| Assign responders | 🔴 Human only | Organizational authority needed |[0m
