## Synthesized Reusable Checklist for deployment-and-rollout SKILL.md

This consolidated checklist can be embedded directly in the SKILL.md as a "Production Readiness — responsible-ai-api Patterns" section:

### Pre-Deployment Safety

```markdown
## Production Readiness Checklist (responsible-ai-api Patterns)

### A. Fail-Open & Kill-Switch
- [ ] Every inference endpoint has a fail-open path gated behind a permanent kill-switch
- [ ] Kill-switch default = safe behaviour (ALLOW for moderation)
- [ ] Kill-switch annotated: `# Owner`, `# Type: kill-switch`, `# Created`, `# Cleanup-by: permanent`
- [ ] Fail-open decision centralised in single function (all endpoints participate)
- [ ] `fail_open.count` metric emitted with `reason` tag at every decision site
- [ ] Fail-open metric on primary dashboard (not log-mining only)
- [ ] Detector/alert threshold for fail-open rate exceeding baseline
- [ ] Cross-cutting-policy lint verifies ALL endpoints are covered

### B. Per-Tenant Rate Limiting
- [ ] Per-tenant token bucket implemented for endpoints with noisy-neighbour risk
- [ ] Bucket keyed on existing `tenant_id` tag (no new identifiers needed)
- [ ] Returns HTTP 429 + `Retry-After` (not 503)
- [ ] `<endpoint>.tenant_throttled.count` metric with `tenant_id` tag
- [ ] Behind default-off feature gate; ramped per-tenant
- [ ] Capacity configured via dynamic config (no-redeploy tuning)
- [ ] Default capacity sized for legitimate large-batch usage
- [ ] Back-off contract socialised with high-volume callers pre-activation
- [ ] Paired with edge-layer rate limiting for defence-in-depth

### C. Multi-Stage Inference (if applicable)
- [ ] Shadow-mode validation completed before any traffic shift
- [ ] Each stage has independent fail-open behaviour
- [ ] Feature gates have corresponding kill-switch for emergency bypass
- [ ] Per-stage metrics enable independent monitoring and alerting
- [ ] Rollout is per-tenant percentage (not per-instance)
- [ ] Stage 1 failure → fall through to Stage 2; Stage 2 failure → fail open

### D. Canary & Progressive Rollout
- [ ] Using `safeReleaseSliver` template (progressive rollout + soak + canary + holidays)
- [ ] Canary configs: `spinnaker-default-4xx` + `spinnaker-default-5xx` + domain-specific
- [ ] `onCanaryAnalysisFailure: rollback` for production
- [ ] Canary cohort verified to span ≥2 AZs
- [ ] `bin/safe-rollback` wrapper preserves ASG Min floor
- [ ] Soak times: ≥30 min pre-prod, ≥60 min first prod region
- [ ] Progressive percentages: [1, 5, 10, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100]
- [ ] Slack channel configured for canary failure notifications
- [ ] Rollback procedure in on-call runbook with exact CLI commands
- [ ] Pollinator checks cover ALL service endpoints
- [ ] Rollback tested in staging before production reliance
- [ ] Post-deployment: verify dashboard green for latency + errors + resources
```

### AI Employee Execution Notes

When an AI employee executes this checklist:
- **Autonomous steps:** Verify metrics exist, check feature gate annotations, validate canary config, verify AZ distribution
- **Human confirmation required:** Activating kill-switch in production, changing capacity limits, socialising contracts with external callers, triggering production rollback
- **Domain terminology:** "fail-open" = return permissive decision on error; "kill-switch" = permanent feature gate (never cleaned up); "token bucket" = rate limiter algorithm with capacity + refill rate; "canary" = small % of production traffic serving new code

