## 7. ML-Specific Incident Patterns

### 7.1 ML System Failure Modes (From Internal Research)

From [ML Observability - High Level Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/4383629681) and [Design: ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349):

| Failure Mode | Detection Method | Typical Severity |
|-------------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Model serving outage (100% errors) | Health check / synthetic probes | Sev1–Sev2 |
| Feature drift (data distribution shift) | KS test, PSI, cosine similarity | Sev3 (unless causing bias) |
| Concept drift (input-output relationship change) | Performance metric degradation | Sev2–Sev3 |
| Inference latency spike (>P99 threshold) | SignalFx detectors | Sev2–Sev3 |
| Model stale (retraining overdue) | ML Lens freshness check | Sev3 |
| Moderation bypass (safety model failure) | Circuit breaker error rate | Sev1–Sev2 |
| Upstream data pipeline failure | Feature freshness monitoring | Sev2–Sev3 |

### 7.2 Drift Detection Statistics

From role doc §4.3 and [Design: ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349):

- **KS Test (Kolmogorov-Smirnov)**: For numerical features — p-value < 0.05 indicates significant drift
- **KL Divergence**: For categorical features — measures distribution shift magnitude
- **Cosine Similarity ≥ 0.60**: NLP embedding floor — below this indicates severe semantic drift
- **Population Stability Index (PSI)**: >0.25 = significant drift requiring investigation

### 7.3 Circuit Breaker Incident Pattern

From role doc §4.1:
- **Threshold**: 20% error rate over 60-second sliding window
- **Action**: Circuit breaker opens → fail-open kill-switch activates
- **This is a Sev2 trigger** if customer-visible moderation/inference fails
- **Automated rollback** should trigger if circuit breaker opens >2times in 15 minutes

### 7.4 How This Applies to ml-incident-response SKILL.md

The skill must include ML-specific classification criteria:
- Drift score thresholds → automatic severity assignment
- Circuit breaker state changes → incident creation triggers
- Model version correlation → link deployment to degradation
- The PIR template should include ML-specific sections: model version, drift scores before/after, feature importance changes, data pipeline state

