## 4. Incident Communication Cadence

### 4.1 Standard Communication Cadence

From [Incident Response Training - Module 2](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~680921421/pages/6813995679) and [Incident Management Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CL1/pages/6205531023):

| Severity | Internal Update Cadence | External (Status Page) Cadence | First External Comms |
|----------|------------------------|-------------------------------|---------------------|
| Sev0/Sev1 | Every 15 min (even "no change") | Every 30 min | Within 20 min of HOT |
| Sev2| Every 15–30 min | Every 30–60 min | Within 20 min of HOT |
| Sev3 | Every 30–60 min | As required | N/A (usually internal only) |

### 4.2 Communication Template Structure

From [Incident Response Training - Module 2](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~680921421/pages/6813995679):

**Initial declaration (within 5 min):**
```
🚨 P[X] declared. [One sentence description]. IC: [Name]. Bridge: [link]. Status page: updated/updating.
```

**Regular updates:**
```
[Timestamp] [Status: Investigating/Identified/Monitoring/Resolved]
- Current impact: [what users are experiencing]
- Mitigation progress: [what we're doing]
- Next steps: [planned actions]
```

**Resolution:**
```
✅ Resolved. [Root cause summary]. Total duration: [X min]. PIR to follow.
```

### 4.3 Status Page Stages

| Stage | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **Investigating** | Issue being assessed |
| **Identified** | Cause or likely cause identified |
| **Monitoring** | Fix applied, recovery being observed |
| **Resolved** | Customer impact ended |

### 4.4 How This Applies to ml-incident-response SKILL.md

- The AI agent must enforce **30-min status cadence** by posting timed updates to the incident Slack thread
- Updates must include: current impact, mitigation progress, next steps
- For ML-specific incidents, updates should include: current error rate, drift score delta, circuit-breaker state, model rollback status
- The AI should surface "silence detected" warnings if no update has been posted for > cadence window
- Human confirmation required (🟡 tier) before posting external communications

---

## 5. Incident Lifecycle Workflow

### 5.1 Standard Phases

From [SRE FY22 Q3 - Incident Management Practices](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IA/pages/1526635958) and [Atlassian Incident Handbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CHILL/pages/254784532):

1. **Detection** — Monitoring/alerting triggers or manual report
2. **Recording** — HOT ticket created in OpsJ with required fields
3. **Classification** — Severity assigned using matrix
4. **Communication** — Stakeholders notified per cadence
5. **Resolution** — Investigation, diagnosis, mitigation, validation
6. **Review** — PIR created, meeting held, actions tracked

### 5.2 Required Incident Data Fields

From [GRC-2915](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/GRC-2915):

All incidents must include:
- Incident start time
- Incident detection time
- Incident end time
- Incident description
- Severity
- Faulty service
- Products affected

Major incidents (Sev2+) PIR additionally requires:
- Impact assessment
- Root cause analysis
- Actions taken
- Approximate number of affected customers
- Affected SLOs (capabilities impacted)

### 5.3 Escalation Decision Framework

From [Understanding Incident Severity](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/5142053110):

- **"When in doubt, escalate, escalate, escalate"** — It's far more impactful to miscategorize as less severe than to upgrade prematurely
- **~50% of Sev3s later convert to Sev2s** — The skill should monitor for upgrade triggers
- Severity changes should happen during incident life, not after resolution
- Peak severity determines PIR requirements

### 5.4 How This Applies to ml-incident-response SKILL.md

The skill workflow should follow this sequence:
1. **Detect** → ML Lens query returns anomaly / SignalFx detector fires / circuit breaker opens
2. **Classify** → Cross-correlate error rate + latency + drift against severity matrix
3. **Record** → Create/update JSM incident ticket with all required fields
4. **Engage** → Page appropriate team based on faulty service mapping
5. **Communicate** → Post initial Slack message, set cadence timer
6. **Mitigate** → Execute runbook (circuit breaker, feature gate, rollback)
7. **Validate** → Confirm metrics returned to normal
8. **Review** → Auto-draft PIR within 5 business days

