## 7. Industry Frameworks Supporting This Design

### Google's ML Production Readiness Rubric
Referenced directly in the [ML Launch Review Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/3611920350): "A Rubric for ML Production Readiness and Technical Debt Reduction" (Google, 2017). Key scoring dimensions:
- **Data quality:** Feature expectations, schema validation, upstream change detection
- **Model staleness:** Retraining cadence, performance degradation detection
- **Monitoring:** Feature drift, prediction drift, latency, error rates
- **Serving:** Fallback mechanisms, gradual rollout, canary analysis

### NIST AI RMF / Google SAIF / ISO 42001
From the `hire_a_tpm` kit documentation: "Risk taxonomy mapped to NIST/Google SAIF/ISO 42001." This validates the multi-dimensional risk assessment approach across:
- Security (SAIF — Secure AI Framework)
- Privacy (NIST AI RMF — AI Risk Management Framework)
- Governance (ISO 42001 — AI Management Systems)

### Atlassian AIMS (AI Management Policy)
The draft [Atlassian AI Management Policy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RM/pages/6851857266) mandates:
- Risk assessments before development, procurement, **deployment**, major change
- Ongoing risk monitoring with documented treatment
- AI Impact Assessments before deployment and when material changes occur

