## 8. Rollback Plan Template

### 8.1 Standard Rollback Decision Matrix

| Trigger | Automated? | Method |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| Canary analysis FAIL (5xx, latency) | ✅ Auto | Spinnaker auto-rollback |
| SignalFx detector fires during progressive rollout | ✅ Auto | Spinnaker auto-rollback |
| Manual operator judgment | ❌ Manual | `atlas micros service rollback -s <svc> -e <env>` |
| Feature flag issue | ❌ Manual | Disable flag in Switcheroo (seconds) |
| Post-deployment SLO breach | ❌ Manual | Rollback if within 1hr; otherwise hotfix |

### 8.2 Rollback Plan Template Structure

```markdown
## Rollback Plan for [Service] [Version]

### Pre-Deployment Checks
- [ ] Previous stack will remain available for at least 1 hour (oldStackLingerTime)
- [ ] Canary analysis configured with appropriate detectors
- [ ] Feature flag kill-switch registered and tested
- [ ] Slack notification channel configured

### Automated Rollback Triggers
- 5xx error rate exceeds [X]% for more than [Y] minutes
- P99 latency exceeds [Z]ms
- Custom detector: [describe metric and threshold]

### Manual Rollback Procedure
1. Verify two stacks still running: `atlas micros service show -s <service>`
2. Scale previous stable stack if needed: `atlas micros compute scale -s <service> -e <env> --deploymentId <id>`
3. Execute rollback: `atlas micros service rollback -s <service> -e <env>`
4. Verify traffic shifted: check Spinnaker UI / SignalFx dashboard
5. Notify team in Slack channel

### If Previous Stack No Longer Available (>1hr)
1. Create revert PR
2. Mark as `[skip-to-prod]` in PR title for fast-track deployment
3. Merge and monitor Spinnaker pipeline

### Post-Rollback
- [ ] Confirm error rate returned to baseline
- [ ] File incident ticket if customer-impacting
- [ ] Update runbook with findings
```

**Source**: [RUNBOOK - Rolling back a service deployment manually](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ServiceMatrix/pages/1222477877), [Deployment Rollback and Rollforward Run Book](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CCG/pages/2459420620)

