## 11. SKILL.md Outline: `deployment-and-rollout`

Based on all research above, here is the proposed outline:

```markdown
# deployment-and-rollout SKILL

## Purpose
Guide the MLE AI employee through deploying ML models and services to production
using the Atlassian internal platform (Spinnaker + Bitbucket Pipelines + Micros),
with feature-flag gating, kill-switches, and automated rollback.

## When to Use
- Deploying a new model version to TEAMServe/Micros
- Setting up or modifying deployment pipelines
- Adding canary analysis or progressive rollout
- Creating rollback plans
- Implementing feature-flag gated rollouts

## Pre-Requisites
- Model validated on Launchpad (ts_lp_launch_validation annotation in ML Registry)
- Load test completed (ts_lp_loadtest_validation annotation)
- Service descriptor validated
- Feature flag registered in Switcheroo

## Workflow Steps

### Step 1: Author Deployment Manifests
- service-descriptor.sd.yml (scaling, resources, env overrides)
- default-pipelines.spinnaker.yaml (template, throughput, canary config)
- canary-config.yml (custom SignalFx detectors if needed)

### Step 2: Configure Feature Flag Gating
- Register kill-switch in Switcheroo/Statsig
- Add flag check in code (fail-open semantics)
- Set rollout strategy based on risk level

### Step 3: Shadow Deployment (Optional but Recommended for ML)
- Deploy shadow endpoint
- Mirror production traffic (read-only)
- Run comparison metrics for N days
- Validate functional parity before canary

### Step 4: Canary/Progressive Rollout
- Choose throughput level (low/high)
- Configure rollout states and soak times
- Enable canary analysis with auto-rollback
- Monitor deployment via Spinnaker UI + SignalFx

### Step 5: Production Validation
- Post-deployment verification (Pollinator synthetic checks)
- Confirm SLO metrics are healthy
- Monitor for N hours during hypercare period

### Step 6: Rollback Plan
- Document automated rollback triggers
- Prepare manual rollback procedure
- Test rollback path before deployment

## Templates
- [Service Descriptor Template]
- [default-pipelines.spinnaker.yaml Template]
- [Canary Config Template]
- [Rollback Plan Template]
- [Production Readiness Checklist]
- [AI/ML Service Safety Checklist (responsible-ai patterns)]

## Human Confirmation Required
- Before first production deployment of a new service
- Before disabling canary analysis overrides
- Before removing feature flag (cleanup)
- When rollback plan involves data migration

## Autonomous Execution Allowed
- Generating deployment manifest from template
- Validating service descriptor
- Creating/updating default-pipelines.spinnaker.yaml
- Registering feature flags
- Monitoring deployment metrics
- Triggering automated rollback via configured thresholds
```

