## 7. Reproduce-From-Registry Workflow

### What Internal Docs Cover
- Tarot v3 lineage tracking: workflow runs → model versions → deployments
- ML Studio: "easy to search and clone existing experiment runs, modify configurations, and trigger new runs"
- Artifacts stored with full metadata in ML Registry

### External Best Practice: Reproducibility Checklist
```
REPRODUCE_FROM_REGISTRY (Day-1Task #1):
  Step 1: Locate model in Tarot v3- Navigate to namespace/component/version
    - Check lineage tab for upstream workflow run
  Step 2: Trace to training workflow
    - Follow lineage to ML Studio workflow run
    - Note: workflow config, dataset version, module versions
  
  Step 3: Re-execute workflow
    - Clone workflow configuration
    - Pin to same dataset version (from `consumes` field)
    - Pin to same module versions
    - Set same random seed
    - Execute on same compute type
  
  Step 4: Validate reproduction
    - Compare metrics: must be within 1% of original (for same seed)
    - Compare model artifacts: hash comparison if deterministic
    - If non-deterministic: multi-seed comparison, metrics within 2σ
  
  Step 5: Document
    - Record: original run ID, reproduction run ID, metric comparison
    - Flag any discrepancies > tolerance
```
- **Source**: ML Model Persistence internal requirements; MLflow reproducibility docs; NIST AI RMF Govern/Map/Measure functions

