─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Source: Live in-workspace repo atlassian_packages/ai-experience-evaluation/
(canonical AIX-eval source).

                                 CLI Surface

 • Binary: aixeval with 3 modes: evaluate | generate | optimise
 • Driven by --config_file (config.yaml) + per-metric-type CLI flags: -iom,
   -diom, -om, -im, -orm (input/output/reference/retrieval shapes)
 • MLflow logging via --log --name; Socrates persistence via --save-data;
   prompt-artefact attach via -sp

                                SDK (Pythonic)

 • LLMEvaluator (evaluation.py) — config-file or RunConfiguration object
   input; programmatic metric add/list
 • Evaluations._run() (workflows/orchestrators.py) — newer
   ExperimentWorkflow-based runner, returns EvaluationResults(results, errors)
   DataFrames; Spark-aware (spark_session= param)
 • FastAPI REST (aixeval_api/) — per-metric endpoints (/bert_score,
   /judge_relevance, etc.) with Pydantic IO models

                        ML-Studio-Native Confirmation

 • Auth via atlassian_ml_studio_sdk.asap + Databricks secret-scope
   (ai-exp-evaluation)
 • Databricks templates: Generate_and_Evaluate_template.py,
   Optimise_and_Evaluate_template.py
 • pip package: atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation==0.1.69
 • Production-data access gated by SSAM group
   socrates-cb-aix-evaluation-dl-users; Socrates upload to zone_ai_experience

                 Metric Taxonomy (~60 evaluators, 12,381 LOC)

8 MetricType shapes (INPUT_OUTPUT, DOUBLE_INPUT_OUTPUT, INPUT, OUTPUT,
OUTPUT_REFERENCE, INPUT_OUTPUT_REFERENCE, INPUT_REFERENCE, RETRIEVAL) ×
ProcessingType (ASYNC/SIMPLE/VECTORIZED). Coverage: NLP reference
(BLEU/ROUGE/BERTScore), LLM-as-judge
(relevance/completeness/conciseness/quality/G-Eval/custom), RAG/retrieval,
factual/safety, ADF integrity, AIFC suite, Jira/Whiteboard/ProactiveAI domain
evals.

               Critical Gaps (the value-add of aix_eval_runner)

AIX-eval does NOT natively enforce role-doc §4.2 rigor:

 1 No multi-seed loop (single-shot per call) → wrapper orchestrates N
   invocations
 2 No k-fold splitter (stratified/time-series/group-aware)
 3 No calibration (ECE/Brier/reliability)
 4 No bootstrap CIs or paired-significance (only mean/median aggregates)
 5 No failure-taxonomy categorization
 6 No slice-by-dimension grouping (rows produced, not auto-sliced)
 7 Reproducibility envelope only partial (MLflow ≠ git SHA + dataset hash +
   CLI string)

                             Proposed Operations

list_metrics, run_evaluation (with stage, seeds, kfold, slice_dimensions,
production_snapshot_id, redaction_policy, baseline_run_id enforcing rigor),
run_generation, run_alpo (cost-bearing), verify_ssam_access,
render_artifact_stub (auto-emit per §10.2 #2).

                                Autonomy Tiers

🟢 offline evals + MLflow log; 🟡 prod-snapshot adhoc + generate + ALPO (token
cost); 🔴 Socrates write of prod-snapshot results + custom-judge in published
reports + headline-metric promotion.

                             Integration Patterns

Composes with rovo_eval_runner (stage 3/5/6 pairing),
experiment_report_generator (consumes results+errors DataFrames),
architecture_comparison_report (paired-run deltas), model_card_generator,
finops_cost_query (joins on model_id+version), mcp__atlassian__ (Confluence
publish), mcp__socrates__ (data lake).

                                 Limitations

Singleton ExperimentConfig cache leakage; JWT 59-min cap (ALPO must refresh or
fail-fast); GPT-OSS uses different gateway URL; errors returned as DataFrame
(must surface as checklist failure, not silently aggregate).


