  Deploy-tool design contract (extracted from rai_hack / responsible-ai-api)

The deploy trio (teamserve_deploy, sagemaker_deploy, triton_endpoint) MUST
follow these 9 patterns verified in the rai_hack codebase:

  1 Canonical TEAMServe gRPC endpoint —
    grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443 (region/env as
    inputs; verified env-var TEAMSERVE_ENDPOINT).
  2 Auth — ASAP JWT via atlassian_jwt_auth.create_signer(reuse_jwts=True) from
    ASAP_ISSUER + ASAP_PRIVATE_KEY (SSAM-provided for agents).
  3 gRPC client — Triton GrpcEndpoint + triton_grpc_client.py with
    TeamservePlugin auth interceptor.
  4 Triton InferInput tensors — typed structured input: input_ids int32
    [1,seq_len], input_lengths, request_output_len, return_generation_logits,
    return_log_probs.
  5 Circuit breaker — production default fail_max=30; surface circuit state in
    errors.
  6 MSP path — /v1/msp/{model-id} via AI Gateway
    (MESH_DEPENDENCY_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL).
  7 CI/CD gate sequence — Build → Test → Deploy DEV (auto) → Deploy STAGING
    (auto) → Deploy PROD (manual + Spinnaker) — never bypass.
  8 Health probes — /healthcheck, /ping, /status.
  9 Per-env defaults via EnvType.{DEV,STAGING,PROD} enum + per-env dict;
    WireMock under Nebulae for test stubs.


