| Get thread replies | `message_get_reply` | Collect incident timeline from Slack thread |
| Search user by email | `workspace_search_user_by_email` | Resolve oncall responder Slack IDs |
| Create channel with members | `workspace_create_channel_with_members` | Create incident war-room channel |
| Get user profile | `get_user` | Retrieve responder details |
| Invite users to channel | `channel_users_invite` | Add escalation responders to incident channel |

**Key Reuse Pattern for Skills:**
- `ml-incident-response` skill uses `channel_create_message` for30-min status cadence posts to incident channel
- `incident_pir_drafter` uses `channel_get_message` + `message_get_reply` to reconstruct incident timeline from Slack
- Drift alert notifications use `channel_create_message` with thread replies for enrichment context

**Capability Gap:** 
- No `conversations.history` with `oldest`/`latest` time-windowed retrieval exposed as MCP tool (needed for extracting incident window messages)
- No message search across workspace by content (only user/channel search) — the Slack MCP currently supports sending and reading but search is via a separate `SlackSchemaAgent` / RTS path

