## 8. JSM Ops REST API for Incidents

### Service Overview
The `jsm-incident-api` is a RESTful microservice (Kotlin, Spring Boot, DynamoDB, SQS) for managing incidents in JSM.

### Key API Endpoints
| Operation | Endpoint | Method |
|-----------|----------|--------|
| Create incident | `/jsm/incidents/cloudId/{cloudId}/v1/incident` | POST |
| Get incident | `/jsm/incidents/cloudId/{cloudId}/v1/incident/{issueID}` | GET |
| Add responders | `/incident/{issueID}/responder/add` | POST |
| Remove responders | `/incident/{issueID}/responder/remove` | POST |
| Add stakeholders | `/incident/{issueID}/stakeholder` | POST |
| Get linked alerts | `/incident/{issueID}/alert` | GET |
| Add linked alerts | `/incident/{issueID}/alert/add` | POST |
| Set major incident | `/incident/{issueID}/major` | POST |
| Affected services | `/incident/{issueID}/service` | POST/DELETE |
| Request status | `/v1/request/{requestId}` | GET |

### Scopes Required
- `read:ops-alert:jira-service-management`
- `write:ops-alert:jira-service-management`
- `read:incident:jira-service-management`
- `write:incident:jira-service-management`

### Incident Status Transitions
Pending → Fixing → Mitigated → Resolved

### Integration with 30-Minute Status Cadence
From SOP-3 and observed PIR patterns:
- Internal communications must be sent within 30-minute SLO
- AI can draft status updates from Slack thread context
