## 1. ML Lens Query API & Drift Detection Statistics

### What It Is
ML Lens is Atlassian's internal ML observability platform providing:
- **Metric ingestion API** for pushing metric values
- **Time-series metric store** (backed by Observo/StarRocks)
- **Alert engine** with Slack/JSM Ops integrations
- **Drift Detection Service** running on ~5-minute cadence

### How It Works — Architecture
```
Feature Logging → ML Lens API → Observo (StarRocks)
                                     ↓
Drift Scheduler (every ~5 min) → SQL aggregation queries
                                     ↓Compute PSI, KS, null%, skewness
                                     ↓
               Write to feature_drift_metrics + Emit alerts
```

### Drift Statistics Supported
| Statistic | Type | Use Case |
|-----------|------|----------|
| **KS test (Kolmogorov-Smirnov)** | Non-parametric | Continuous feature distribution shift |
| **PSI (Population Stability Index)** | Information-theoretic | Overall distribution stability |
| **Chi-squared** | Parametric | Categorical feature drift |
| **KL divergence** | Information-theoretic | Probability distribution divergence |
| **Cosine similarity ≥ 0.60** | NLP embedding floor | Embedding/text feature drift |
| **Summary stats** | Descriptive | mean, stddev, min, max, skewness, kurtosis |
| **Quality metrics** | Operational | null%, zero%, schema conformance |

### Alert Configuration Pattern (from MLFS SDK)
```python
AlertConfig(alert_namespace="my-team.features", alert_key="drift").alert_message("Drift detected in feature distributions.")
    .runbook("<runbook_url>")
    .alert_config(
        AlertMetricConfig(metric_namespace="feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue")
        .condition(AlertCondition.single(Condition(measure="expected_value", operator="<=", value=0.05)))
        .tag_filter("feature_name", "=", "daily_transaction_count")
        .tag_filter("feature_service", "=", "fraud_detection_v2")
    )
    .recipient(Recipient.slack(RecipientValue(id="#ml-alerts", type="channel")))
```

### How It Applies to `ml_lens_queries` Tool
The tool should expose operations for:
1. **Query drift metrics** — fetch PSI/KS/cosine scores for specified features over time windows
2. **Get alert status** — retrieve active drift alerts for a service/model
3. **Query reference comparison** — compare current vs. reference distribution stats
4. **Thresholds**: KS p-value ≤ 0.05 (drift detected), PSI > 0.2 (significant shift), cosine < 0.60 (NLP embedding floor)

**Autonomy**:🟢 Read-only queries are fully autonomous. Alert threshold modifications are🟡 confirm-required.

**Source**: [ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349), [MLFS Feature Observability Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6515785986)

