Key findings:


 1 Mitchell-9 canonical sections for model cards: Model Details, Intended Use,
   Factors, Metrics, Evaluation Data, Training Data, Quantitative Analyses,
   Ethical Considerations, Caveats & Recommendations. Non-negotiable:
   disaggregated + intersectional sub-group metrics; classification →
   FP/FN/FDR/FOR; regression → mean/median/variance/range (aligns with
   role-doc §4.2 mean±std rigor).
 2 Gebru-7 canonical sections (~57 questions) for datasheets: Motivation,
   Composition, Collection Process, Preprocessing/Cleaning/Labeling, Uses,
   Distribution, Maintenance. Deliberately not automated — designed to capture
   creator-only knowledge; supports "Unknown to authors" answers and
   skip-section logic.
 3 Reference implementations to lift primitives from:
    • Google MCT: protobuf+JSON schema, Jinja2 HTML/Markdown templates,
      figure_to_base64str, MLMD auto-populate, TFX ModelCardGenerator (now in
      tfx-addons).
    • VerifyML (MCT fork): adds fairness_analysis, explainability_analysis,
      Test abstraction, and a compare template — direct precedent for
      architecture_comparison_report.
    • Hugging Face: YAML-front-matter + Markdown body via
      huggingface_hub.ModelCard; model-index for eval results;
      metadata_update(overwrite=, create_pr=) semantics for partial updates.
    • Wayflyer pattern: Pydantic + Jinja2 (no protoc) — recommended over MCT
      protobuf for AI-employee-friendly schema evolution.
 4 Proposed combined schema merges Mitchell-9 + Gebru-7 + role-doc additions:
   cost_section (FinOps), deployment_manifest_ref (§10.5
   intent/non-goals/invariants/risk/rollback), explicit statistical-rigor
   fields (CIs, calibration, failure_taxonomy, negative_results),
   disclosure_level per-section enum (full/aggregate/redacted), changelog for
   versioning (Perspective v1↔v5 pattern), source: {tool, run_id} per section
   for idempotent regenerate-with-diff.
 5 Render targets: Confluence HTML (via mcp__atlassian__), HF-compatible
   Markdown, JSON/Protobuf (for diffing), PDF, Slack blocks (for
   weekly_experiment_digest).
 6 Gaps neither framework covers that the generator must fill: FinOps cost
   section, deployment-manifest cross-link, explicit statistical-rigor
   structured fields, SageMaker→TEAMServe migration deltas, multi-turn/ConvoAI
   per-trajectory metrics.
 7 Integration pattern: rovo_eval_runner / aix_eval_runner / finops_cost_query
   / experiment_report_generator → canonical JSON contract → consumed by
   architecture_comparison_report, weekly_experiment_digest,
   deployment_manifest_generator. Reserve human-fill for out_of_scope_uses,
   potential_harms, recommended_next_steps with LLM [suggested] drafts.
 8 Open questions surfaced: datasheet embedded vs separate-artifact; Aether
   template adoption; Croissant dual-emission; Pydantic+Jinja vs protobuf-MCT
   path (recommend Pydantic).
