### Tool: `signalfx_detector_iac`
*Purpose: Manage SignalFx detectors as Terraform code via Sauron + Bitbucket pipeline*

**Context from workspace research**: Atlassian uses Sauron (internal Terraform wrapper) to manage SignalFx detectors as IaC. Changes are deployed via Bitbucket PRs → `terraform plan` on PR → `terraform apply` on master merge. The standard pattern is: `.tf` files in `operations/terraform/`, `.sauron.yml` config, pipeline-automated deployment.

| Action | Tier | Rationale |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Read existing detector definitions (list, describe) | 🟢 | Read-only; inspecting current IaC state |
| Run `terraform plan` (dry-run preview of changes) | 🟢 | Non-destructive; preview only; standard PR workflow |
| Generate new detector `.tf` definition (draft, not applied) | 🟢 | File creation in branch; no production impact until merged |
| Open PR with new/modified detector code | 🟡 | Creates reviewable artifact; bounded to single service; "two-way door" (PR can be declined); but touches production alerting pipeline |
| Add detector for a new signal (e.g., new5xx rate alarm) | 🟡 | Increases observability coverage; low-risk but novel pattern; needs human review of threshold calibration |
| Modify existing detector thresholds | 🟡 | Could suppress real alerts or create noise; "two-way door" (revertible) but impacts on-call experience |
| Delete/disable a detector | 🔴 | Reduces observability coverage; could mask outages; "one-way door" in terms of missed alerts during gap period |
| Modify SLO definitions in IaC (TOME SLO targets) | 🔴 | Policy-defining action; changes error budget calculations; org-level reporting impact |
| Bulk-modify multiple detectors across services | 🔴 | Unbounded blast radius; cross-service impact; requires coordinated human review |

