## 2. Per-Tool Autonomy Tier Assignments

### Tool: `ml_lens_queries`
*Purpose: Read production metrics, drift statistics, model health signals from ML Lens*

| Action | Tier | Rationale |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Query drift metrics (KS, PSI, KL divergence) | 🟢 | Read-only; bounded query; no state mutation |
| Query feature distributions (current vs. reference) | 🟢 | Read-only aggregate statistics |
| Query model quality metrics (NDCG, precision@K) | 🟢 | Read-only; existing dashboard surface |
| Query cosine similarity for NLP embeddings | 🟢 | Read-only; standard statistical test |
| Query alert history and status | 🟢 | Read-only; operational awareness |
| Compare drift across time windows (training baseline, 30d rolling) | 🟢 | Read-only cross-reference |
| Generate drift summary report | 🟢 | Synthesis of read-only data |
| Trigger ad-hoc drift computation job | 🟡 | Consumes compute resources; could impact ML Studio cluster; novel trigger pattern |
| Modify alert thresholds in ML Lens | 🔴 | Changes alerting policy; could mask production degradation; policy-defining action |

