### Tool: `circuit_breaker_control`
*Purpose: Operate circuit breaker state and configuration for responsible-ai-api + ML-Engine*

**Context from ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook** (https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626):
- Config: TIME_BASED,60s window, ≥20calls,20% failure threshold, 30s base wait (exponential to 60s max)
- Fail-open pattern: service continues serving when CB opens (graceful degradation)
- Kill-switch via feature gate targeting

| Action | Tier | Rationale |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Read circuit breaker state (OPEN/CLOSED/HALF_OPEN) | 🟢 | Read-only operational awareness |
| Read current CB configuration parameters | 🟢 | Read-only |
| Query CB transition history and trip frequency | 🟢 | Read-only; aids pattern analysis |
| Activate fail-open kill-switch (disable CB for specific tenant) | 🟢 | **Bounded blast radius** — single tenant isolation; runbook-documented recovery pattern; known safe action during confirmed outage; auto-reverts when underlying cause resolves; matches SOP "consider temporarily disabling CB for unaffected tenants" |
| Reset CB from OPEN to CLOSED (force recovery probe) | 🟡 | Could re-expose traffic to unhealthy downstream; bounded to single service instance; reversible but requires monitoring confirmation |
| Tune CB thresholds (raise/lower failureRateThreshold, slidingWindowSize) | 🟡 | Impacts sensitivity; requires canary rollout per runbook ("5-10% traffic, monitor for two windows"); "two-way door" but affects reliability posture |
| Enable/disable circuit breaker entirely | 🔴 | Removes protection layer; unbounded blast radius; "one-way door" during the gap (cascading failures possible); requires Tech Lead + SRE + PM approval per runbook §3|
| Change fail-open kill-switch policy (global, not per-tenant) | 🔴 | Policy-defining; affects entire service behavior during failures; organizational risk if misconfigured |
| Modify the failure predicate (what counts as failure) | 🔴 | Redefines the meaning of "failure"; could make CB blind to real outages or hyper-sensitive; fundamental policy change |
| Automated rollback trigger (ASG floor preservation) | 🟡 | Bounded blast radius (single deployment); well-defined runbook pattern; but involves infrastructure state change |

