### Tool: `incident_pir_drafter`
*Purpose: Draft Post-Incident Reviews for JSM incidents following Atlassian PIR templates*

**Context from PIR Action Validation Logic** (https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/6434888493) and SOP-3 (TTD<15m, TTR<2h, 30-min status cadence, PIR<5BD):

| Action | Tier | Rationale |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Gather incident timeline from JSM/Slack/Splunk | 🟢 | Read-only data collection |
| Correlate signals across monitoring systems | 🟢 | Read-only cross-reference |
| Generate PIR draft skeleton (summary, timeline, root cause, actions) | 🟢 | Document creation in draft state; no publication; matches "Operations Lead" role from Google SRE ICS model |
| Post30-min status cadence update to incident Slack channel | 🟢 | Known SOP pattern; bounded communication; supplements (not replaces) human IC updates; auto-generated from current facts |
| Calculate TTD/TTR metrics from incident timestamps | 🟢 | Deterministic calculation from data |
| Suggest severity classification based on impact matrix | 🟡 | Classification recommendation; human confirms before application; wrong severity → wrong response resources |
| File PIR draft to Confluence (publish for review) | 🟡 | Creates visible organizational artifact; requires human review before stakeholder distribution; "two-way door" (page can be edited/unpublished) |
| Link PIR action items as Jira tickets | 🟡 | Creates work items with assignees; scoped to single incident; reversible (tickets can be cancelled) |
| Assign severity to live incident | 🔴 | Directly affects escalation, resourcing, and communication scope; wrong assignment could under-resource a real outage or over-alert on noise |
| Trigger escalation (page additional responders) | 🔴 | Human cost — wakes people up; reputation impact if false; irreversible disruption; must remain human IC decision |
| Approve/close PIR (mark review complete) | 🔴 | Organizational sign-off; carries accountability implications; must be human decision per Incident Response Plan |
| Modify incident response process/runbook | 🔴 | Policy-defining change; affects all future incidents; requires broad review |

