   (sha256(workflow_id||step_index||run_id||payload_hash), 24h dedup window),
   uniform retry/no-retry classification (HTTP/gRPC), 5-in-60s circuit
   breaker, and a parallel-launch contract declaring kind, primitive,
   max_in_flight, and explicit sop_sizing.
 2 Per-tool scopes (§§2–11) — Full draft scopes for mlflow_run_manager,
   ml_studio_training_job, optimus_prime_hpo, tarot_v3_registry,
   tecton_mlfs_features, teamserve_deploy, sagemaker_deploy (flagged as
   possible sunset), triton_endpoint, feature_flag_rollout (composed-only by
   default), and launchpad_preprod. Each lists operation-level inputs/outputs,
   idempotency rules, autonomy tier (🟢/🟡/🔴), and rate limits.
 3 Parallel-launch sizing (§12.3) — ml_studio_training_job.parallel_submit is
   the primary native primitive for both SOP-1 step 3 (2–4 architectures, hard
   cap 10) and SOP-2 step 5 (5–10 variants).
   optimus_prime_hpo.create_sweep(max_parallel=5..10) is the alternate native
   primitive for SOP-2 hyperparameter cycles. Downstream tools (Tarot,
   TEAMServe, SageMaker, Triton, Launchpad) only need agent-driven fan-out
   (gather with semaphores) because eval narrows to a single winner before
   deploy.
 4 gRPC/MSP integration — teamserve_deploy codifies the canonical
   grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443 endpoint,
   region/env matrix, gRPC-status-aware retry, (deployment_id, ramp_label)
   idempotency for traffic splits, server-side same-region serialization,
   multi-region parallel deploys, and an auto-rollback trigger encoding
   responsible-ai-api canary patterns. Recommends vendoring the
   responsible-ai-api gRPC client + ruamel.yaml-based MSP descriptor loader
   rather than re-implementing.
 5 Cross-cutting matrices (§12) — Tabulated auth credentials, idempotency
   keys, parallel-launch capacities, and autonomy tiers across all 10 tools
   for direct aggregator consumption.
 6 Open questions (§14) — Slauth audiences for Optimus Prime / Tarot v3 / MLFS
   / Launchpad need confirmation; mcp__switcheroo__ rollout-percentage gap
   should be verified via get_tool_schema before shipping feature_flag_rollout
   as a standalone tool; TEAMServe .proto and cost-estimate API need locating.
 7 AI considerations (§15) — Uniform retry/circuit-break pseudocode;
   validate-first, checkpoint-after-side-effect, indefinite-block on 🔴 human
   gates, mandatory lineage propagation (training_run_uuid → 
   tarot_model_version → deployment_id → flag_id → build_sha) through every
   downstream call.


