─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Full report written to outputs/facet.md.

                                 Key findings

1. Canonical TEAMServe endpoint URL templates (validated in repo)

 • gRPC host: grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net (port :443
   implicit via tritonclient.grpc.InferenceServerClient(url=…, ssl=True)).
   Tokens observed: region ∈ {us-east-1, us-west-2}, env ∈ {dev, stg, prod}.
   Set as TEAMSERVE_ENDPOINT env var; defaulted in src/config.py:125 and
   overridden per‑env in archetype-descriptor.yaml.
 • HTTP/Tarot host:
   https://teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net/v1/models/tarot/{nam
   espace}/versions/{version}/v1/chat/completions (used for
   GPT‑OSS/OpenAI‑compatible calls).

2. Auth model is ASAP, audience teamserve
atlassian_jwt_auth.create_signer(..., reuse_jwts=True). Headers injected by
TeamservePlugin on every gRPC request: x-teamserve-model,
x-teamserve-model-version, x-teamserve-source, authorization: Bearer <JWT>.
For httpx there is a custom _HttpxJWTAuth(httpx.Auth) adapter (needed because
the shipped JWTAuth returns bytes which httpx rejects).

3. Resilience contract —
pybreaker.CircuitBreaker(name="triton_circuit_breaker", fail_max=30) wraps
every call; gRPC timeout=5s/client_timeout=6s; HTTP pool MAX_CONNECTIONS=1024,
KEEPALIVE_EXPIRY_SECONDS=90 (under TeamServe’s 100‑120 s server keepalive).
Switcheroo gate rai_enable_httpxclient toggles pooled httpx vs legacy
requests; gate eval failures never propagate (silent fallback).

4. MSP / Micros service-descriptor patterns

 • Authoritative descriptor is archetype-descriptor.yaml (schemaVersion
   1.1.0), synthesised at build time via ./bin/synth-sd + envsubst
   (POCO_LABEL, DOCKER_TAG, DOCKER_IMAGE) → build-output/service.sd.yml.
 • Key sections any deploy tool must encode:
   serviceProxy{ingress.auth.asap+usercontext, egress.dependencies, 
   plugins.authorization.poco}, loadBalancer{ALB, least_outstanding_requests},
   links.healthcheck, notifications.email, computeClassification.dataType,
   compose.microservice + compose.statsig-sidecar, environmentOverrides per
   env, and resources of type slauth-gateway, sm-endpoint (SageMaker —
   first-class), cloudformation (nlb-endpoint-service-v2 for PrivateLink),
   continuous-chaos.
 • Spinnaker rollout is encoded in default-pipelines.spinnaker.yaml using
   template: safeRelease, environments adev → stg-east → prod-east,
   progressive rollout only on staging, serviceDescriptorTag: 
   service-descriptor, two role grants.
 • Minimal "register a Tarot/TEAMServe model" descriptor template is
   model_onboarding/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b/deployment/rai-gptoss.sd.yml
   (description, links.healthcheck=/health, notifications, organization,
   compose.microservice{image, tag, ports}, buildNumber).
 • Feature flags wired through Statsig server sidecar
   (docker.atl-paas.net/sox/atlassian/statsig-sidecar:stable-v2, HTTP_LISTEN:
   0.0.0.0:6061) + Features enum + _check_gate() in src/feature_service.py.

5. Wrapper‑vs‑new decision (this repo only)

 • Wrap: teamserve_deploy (gRPC and HTTP), sagemaker_deploy (use MSP
   sm-endpoint), launchpad_preprod (patch safeRelease yaml),
   feature_flag_rollout (codegen into Features enum + ensure sidecar block).
 • New impl needed: tarot_v3_registry (no programmatic Tarot client exists in
   repo — URLs are string‑built).
 • Out of scope here (not referenced in responsible-ai-api):
   mlflow_run_manager, ml_studio_training_job, optimus_prime_hpo,
   tecton_mlfs_features.

6. Gaps / constraints

 • Region/env values are hard-coded per env override; no GCP region tokens
   exist for TEAMServe. A composer tool should fail closed on unknown {region,
   env} pairs.
 • AtlasKube variant (responsible-ai-api-gcp) requires explicit MICROS_ENVTYPE
   and MICROS_SERVICE_DOMAIN_NAME — not auto-injected.
 • service.sd.yml is never checked in; consumers must run ./bin/synth-sd or
   model the YAML-anchor + environmentOverrides merge.
 • Triton model name/version is hard-coded (teamserve-rai-optimized-logits /
   1) in TeamserveGrpcBackend; tool spec should parameterise.


