Key findings:


 1 RovoDev HTML format (not Confluence storage XML) is mandatory — the
   confluence skill explicitly rejects <ac:...> / <ri:...> macros. All
   generators must emit HTML using documented patterns: <div 
   data-type="panel-info|warning|note|success|error">, <span 
   data-type="status">, <ul data-type="decision-list">, <ul 
   data-type="task-list">, <details> for expands, <section 
   data-type="layout-two-equal"> for columns, <pre><code 
   class="language-mermaid"> for diagrams, and <div data-type="chart" 
   data-chart-type="LINE|BAR|AREA|PIE|DONUT"> wrapping a <table> for charts.
 2 Reusable primitives (so generators only encode layout/content):
    • Templating sink: create_confluence_page / file-based
      update_confluence_page workflow with version_message audit trail;
      live-doc mode for the weekly digest.
    • Discovery: search_confluence_using_cql with label = "ml-experiment" AND
      lastModified > now("-7d").
    • Scheduling:
      mcp__slack__slack_create_scheduled_message(postAt=unix_seconds) for
      digest announcements.
    • Query: mcp__socrates__create_query (async submit-poll) for all cost /
      eval rollups.
    • Context: mcp__rovodev__get_full_context_for_user,
      mcp__feedback__search_feedback*, TWG get_context_for_work_item for
      linked PRs/commits.
 3 Four templates designed with required inputs and full HTML skeletons:
    • experiment_report_generator — [EXP] titled, with 6-stage method table,
      mean±std results with 95% CI, fairness chart, calibration, failure
      taxonomy, top-level "Negative Results" section (never collapsed),
      customer-signal sidebar, reproducibility expand.
    • architecture_comparison_report — [ADR] titled, weighted comparison
      matrix, per-rejected-alternative deep dives at equal detail with Mermaid
      diagrams, decision list, supersedes-link mechanism that auto-updates
      prior ADR status.
    • weekly_experiment_digest — [DIGEST] titled, live-doc, two-column TL;DR
      (landed / negative), three-column cost stewardship cards, 8-week line
      chart, experiment table, customer signal, Slack scheduled ping at Monday
      09:00.
    • deployment_manifest_generator — [MANIFEST] titled, mirrors role §10.5
      fields (intent + non-goals + invariants + risks + rollback), eval-gate
      evidence table, likelihood×impact risk matrix, Mermaid timeline ramp
      plan, executable rollback steps with verification task list, sign-off
      task list with @mentions.
 4 Cross-cutting conventions: machine-readable banner panel, status lozenge in
   header, idempotent [TAG] title prefix → CQL discovery contract,
   mention-based notification delivery, reproducibility footer in every page.
 5 Gaps: no HTML-level label attribute (use [TAG] prefix + post-create REST
   label call), no Confluence-native scheduler (must use AI-employee
   scheduler), Mermaid requires Forge app (degrade to ASCII), expand/table
   cannot self-nest (use nested-expand-in-<td>), Feedback MCP needs spaceAri
   config per team.
 6 Autonomy: all read ops fully autonomous; write ops require user
   confirmation unless generator invoked explicitly; Socrates async with
   exponential backoff (2s→30s, max 5min); Confluence 409 → re-fetch &
   re-apply.
