─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Reusable primitives discovered:

 • mcp__atlassian__ Confluence: create_confluence_page /
   update_confluence_page accept HTML (file paths) — translated to ADF by
   validator. Supports panels (info/warning/note/success/error), task lists,
   tables, mermaid, layouts, expanders, status lozenges, dates, smart links.
   All eight artifact generators can emit HTML and rely on this single sink.
   version_message provides audit trail; add_confluence_page_comment supports
   inline + footer. search_confluence_using_cql for de-dup pre-checks.
 • mcp__slack__: slack_create_scheduled_message(channelId, text, postAt[unix],
   threadTs) is the native cadence primitive — enables weekly digest / daily
   standup automation. channel_create_message supports limited HTML subset
   (<b>, <i>, <a>, <ul>, <li>, <p>, <br>, <pre>, <code> — no tables).
   workspace_search_user_by_email for owner @mentions.
 • mcp__rovodev__: get_full_context_for_user is a ready-made digest collector;
   get_similar_issues anchors negative-results discipline; get_loom_video
   returns transcripts for model card embedding; atlassian_search 
   RELATIONSHIPS uses Teamwork Graph.
 • mcp__feedback__: search_chunk is hybrid semantic+filter — powers
   qualitative sections in model cards and cost stewardship.
   search_feedback_count for headline metrics. Use saved viewId over inline
   filters when PMs have curated.
 • mcp__socrates__: create_query(sql) returns statementId for async;
   get_query_status to poll. Sole production-data path for FinOps + eval data.
   Gap: no flow scheduling — only read. Generators must own SQL template
   library + polling helper.

Critical gaps (must be net-new):

 1 No recurring SQL/flow scheduling — must live in Symphony / external cron.
 2 No native topic clustering over feedback — generator must LLM-cluster.
 3 No chart rendering primitive beyond mermaid — generate PNG + upload as
   attachment.
 4 No cancel-scheduled-Slack-message primitive — design for idempotency.
 5 No cross-product transactionality — order: Confluence → Jira → Slack (Slack
   is point-of-no-return).
 6 mcp__teamwork_graph__ is richer than mcp__rovodev__ for stakeholder/team
   aggregation — adopt as data layer of choice.

Composition patterns to encode in ml-stakeholder-reporting skill:

 1 Rich-artifact + cadence-beacon: create_confluence_page →
   slack_create_scheduled_message carrying URL. Always pair.
 2 Read → mutate → write idempotent: get_confluence_page(output_file) → edit →
   update_confluence_page(version_message) for living docs.
 3 Shared "experiment context bundle": TWG get_context_for_work_item + rovodev
   get_similar_issues + get_loom_video — encode once, reuse across
   experiment_report, weekly_digest, model_card, architecture_comparison.

Skill precedent:
_dev/tpm_ai_lab_skills_tools/skills/confluence-program-docs/SKILL.md provides
the structural template — front-matter (name, description, labels,
metadata.tools), then numbered Workflow Mappings with step-by-step tool calls.
Caveat: the existing adf-template-catalog.md encodes ADF JSON, but our
Confluence MCP takes HTML — port templates to HTML.

Build-vs-reuse map for all 8 tools and 3 skills is fully tabulated in §8 of
the report. Net-new logic is concentrated in: rigor checklist enforcement,
FinOps SQL library, statistical aggregators (mean±std, k-fold, calibration,
CIs, fairness slicing), §10.5 deployment manifest template, and
negative-results discipline templates.


AI autonomy notes: All reads + explicitly-requested writes are autonomous;
proactive Jira filings and any cost-stewardship deployment throttling are Tier
🔴 / confirm-first. Socrates async needs an exponential-backoff helper (not
built-in). Confluence concurrent edits are last-write-wins — mitigate with CQL
precheck + version_message.
