 1 Reference definition of §10.5 3-tier autonomy model — 🟢 (auto/observe,
   read-only or sandboxed, reversible, no approver), 🟡 (recommend/propose,
   writes to shared spaces, rotation approver), 🔴 (restricted, prod
   traffic/cost-affecting or customer-facing, named approver + audit).
   Orthogonal to L1–L5 maturity.
 2 Per-operation tier matrix for all 8 artifacts + 2 runners
   (rovo_eval_runner, aix_eval_runner, finops_cost_query,
   model_card_generator, experiment_report_generator,
   architecture_comparison_report, weekly_experiment_digest,
   deployment_manifest_generator). Tiers are assigned per operation (not per
   tool), with rationale and reversibility. Highlights: 6-stage eval protocol
   maps to escalating tiers (stages 1–3 🟢, 4–5 🟡, 6 🔴);
   aix_eval.with_production_data is 🟡 (cannot be 🔴 without breaking §4.2
   capability); all generator draft ops are 🟢, publish-to-shared-space are
   🟡, publish-to-public/leadership or mark-canonical are 🔴;
   deployment_manifest.attach-to-deploy --prod is 🔴.
 3 Tier-as-computed-function rule — tier should be derived from
   affects_prod_traffic, affects_cost > $100/day, writes_to_shared_space,
   opens_pr booleans on each operation, rather than free-form labels. Prevents
   drift and gaming.
 4 Negative-results documentation built into every generator via:
    • Mandatory schema fields in every artifact (result_class,
      hypothesis_status, failure_taxonomy, what_we_learned,
      recommended_next_step, plus seeds/CIs/calibration/slices/cost) — lint
      fails the build if missing on negatives.
    • Per-generator hooks — model card "Known Failure Modes" section,
      experiment_report --negative-result first-class mode,
      architecture_comparison mandatory "Variants we eliminated" table,
      weekly_digest "What didn't work" section with at-least-one-entry rule
      (else lint warning), deployment_manifest auto-cites gating negatives in
      Risks, eval runners always emit a report even on failure (never silent
      CI red), finops emits "do-not-migrate" RFCs at equal rigor.
    • Anti-pattern guardrails — block re-labelling as "inconclusive" without
      n_runs≥5 + CI proof, block missing failure_taxonomy, track per-author
      draft-to-publish ratio for audit, force above-the-fold rendering.
 5 Cross-skill ownership — ml-stakeholder-reporting owns the AutonomyTier enum
   + artifact header template + negative-results schema;
   ml-evaluation-elevated-standards owns lint rules + failure-taxonomy vocab;
   ml-cost-stewardship owns the cost block (incl. experimentation cost for
   negatives).
 6 Aggregator checklist of six concrete items the subtask-3 aggregator must
   verify (tool.json operations[] schema, canonical enum location, lint rules,
   cost block, banner injection, CI parity test for negative vs. positive
   publishing path).


