Key Findings


 1 Anti-duplication seam with worker_1 (build-side) is clean — worker_1 owns
   MLflow, Tarot v3 registry, training, packaging, deployment, Launchpad,
   feature store, Unity Catalog. Sibling worker_18 owns ML Lens, SignalFx,
   circuit-breaker, PIR drafter, Launch-Review gate, Symphony/ORBIT. Worker_19
   is exclusively read+template generators over data those other workers
   produce — zero capability overlap.
 2 Reusable in-workspace primitives identified (no need to rebuild):
    • mcp__atlassian__ Confluence: create/update_confluence_page, plus rich
      HTML format (panels, chart-wrapped tables, Mermaid, expand, status
      lozenges, decision/task lists, two-equal layouts, live docs) — covers
      ALL artifact-rendering needs for the 6 generators.
    • mcp__slack__create_scheduled_message(channelId, text, postAt) —
      implements weekly-Monday-9am digest cadence with no cron.
    • mcp__socrates__create_query + get_query_status — full async SQL path for
      finops_cost_query; only the curated SQL templates are net-new.
    • mcp__rovodev__get_full_context_for_user(from_date, to_date) —
      foundational primitive for weekly_experiment_digest (returns 7-day
      Confluence/Jira/PR work context out of the box); also get_recent_prs,
      atlassian_search, atlassian_docs_search, get_similar_issues,
      get_loom_video.
    • mcp__feedback__ (search/count/chunk) — production-impact +
      failure-taxonomy seeding for experiment reports & model cards.
    • mcp__google_drive__ (workspace_create_document, create_spreadsheet,
      update_spreadsheet_values, permissions, comments) — alternate
      distribution path for external stakeholders.
 3 Net-new surface — purely templating/composition: each of the 8
   generator/runner tools and 3 skills only needs to encode the missing
   layout/content logic (HTML templates, rigor checklist render, autonomy-tier
   badges, negative-results sections, SQL library, cadence rules).
 4 CLI/SDK wrappers required (no existing MCP): rovo-eval and AIX-eval need
   fresh wrappers that emit a standardized result JSON (per-seed metrics,
   mean±std, per-slice, failure-taxonomy histogram, calibration points, CI
   bounds, 6-stage tag).
 5 §10.5 autonomy-tier mapping: All read/query and bounded-publish actions are
   🟢; production-data sampling, new-channel publishing, and arbitrary-parent
   page creates are 🟡; kill-switch policy changes in deployment manifests are
   🔴.
 6 Negative-results discipline: Every generator must take is_negative_result
   flag, use identical template, publish to same parent location, auto-tag
   with ml-negative-result Confluence label, and link bidirectionally with the
   successful approach's artifacts.
 7 Composition patterns documented for weekly digest, model-card production,
   and deployment-manifest assembly — each is a chain across worker_1
   build-side outputs + worker_18 ops outputs + worker_19 generators +
   Confluence/Slack distribution.
 8 Error-handling/retry primitives already exist: async-poll for Socrates,
   read-before-write for Confluence updates, CQL existence check before
   create, Slack scheduled-message idempotency via cached
   scheduled_message_id.
