## Original User Request
**Description**: Create skills and tools that enable the AI MLE to perform the OPERATE-SIDE of the ML lifecycle: production observability, drift detection, reliability engineering, incident response, evaluation execution with elevated standards, cost/capacity tracking, and stakeholder communication / governance discipline. This cluster shares observability + Atlassian SDLC API clients (ML Lens, SignalFx, JSM Ops, Slack, Confluence, Bitbucket) and covers responsibilities #1, #7, #8, #9, #10 plus Symphony/ORBIT governance.

Proposed new tools (validate against subtask 1):
- `ml_lens_queries` — query drift metrics (KS test, KL divergence, cosine similarity), data-quality dashboards, model-performance and system-health dashboards; supports the cosine ≥ 0.60 NLP-embedding floor [role doc §4.3, §9].
- `signalfx_detector_iac` — author/update SignalFx detectors-as-code, encode per-endpoint SLOs in IaC [§2 #7, §5.1].
- `circuit_breaker_control` — activate/inspect ML-Engine circuit breakers (20% / 60s sliding-window threshold), fail-open kill-switches, automated rollback within rehearsed scope [§4.1, §10.5 🟢].
- `incident_pir_drafter` — auto-draft PIRs within 5 BD from reasoning traces (TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC, gaps, prevention, playbook updates) — emits to Confluence + JSM Ops [§4.1, §6 SOP-3 step 7].
- `rovo_eval_runner` and `aix_eval_runner` — execute end-to-end agent quality evals (ConvoAI multi-turn) and pythonic ML-Studio-native evals with production-data access [§4.2].
- `ml_launch_review_gate` — encode the ML Launch Review Checklist as automated gates (privacy review, rollback plan, drift monitor, alerting) [§4.1].
- `finops_cost_query` — query FinOps dashboards and ML Artifact Cost Monitoring for inference cost/request, GPU utilization, training cost per version; supports SageMaker→TEAMServe migration analysis pattern [§4.3, §5 cost stewardship].
- `model_card_generator`, `experiment_report_generator`, `architecture_comparison_report`, `weekly_experiment_digest`, `deployment_manifest_generator` — template-driven artifact emission to Confluence/Slack; all generated as byproducts of work per §7.3 / §10.2 #2 (negative results documented with equal rigor).
- `symphony_orbit_enrichment` — append outcomes (experiment results, incidents, runbook updates) to ORBIT context layer; honors autonomy-tier gating.

Proposed new skills:
- `ml-production-monitoring-and-drift` — guidance for 24/7 portfolio monitoring, drift triage, automated rollback, fallback patterns; orchestrates `ml_lens_queries` + `circuit_breaker_control` + `signalfx_detector_iac`.
- `ml-incident-response` — guidance for SOP-3 (TTD < 15 min, TTR < 2 h, 30-min status cadence, severity classification, cross-correlation, escalation rules); uses `incident_pir_drafter`, JSM Ops, Slack.
- `ml-evaluation-elevated-standards` — guidance encoding non-negotiable rigor: failure-taxonomy categorization, mean±std across seeds, full k-fold (stratified/time-series/group-aware), slice-by-every-dimension, calibration + CIs + fairness, comprehensive error analysis [§4.2, §10.2 #4, §10.2 #6]; orchestrates the eval runners.
- `ml-stakeholder-reporting` — guidance for weekly digests, model cards, experiment reports, architecture comparison reports (incl. rejected alternatives), quarterly impact narrative; uses the generator tools.
- `ml-symphony-governance` — guidance for 3-tier autonomy (🟢/🟡/🔴), deployment-manifest discipline (intent + non-goals + invariants + risk + rollback), calibrated-uncertainty communication (80%=80%), policy compliance, L1–L5 maturity progression [§10.5].
- `ml-cost-stewardship` — guidance for cost/capacity tracking, infra migration recommendations, per-experiment compute budget enforcement.

Research requirement: investigate existing Atlassian-internal ML Lens / SignalFx / JSM Ops / Slack / Confluence / FinOps APIs and any existing rovo-eval / AIX-eval CLIs. Examine `responsible-ai-api` runbook (role doc §4.1) and ML-Engine circuit breaker runbook for the exact patterns to encode. Pay particular attention to each runbook/playbook in §4.1 as candidate automation tools, each query pattern in §4.3 as candidate retrieval tools, and each eval framework in §4.2 as a candidate validation tool — per task instruction.

**Todos**:
- Research ML Lens, SignalFx, JSM Ops, Slack, Confluence, Bitbucket, FinOps, rovo-eval, AIX-eval APIs/SDKs; document existing wrappers and gaps.
- Draft tool.json for each operational tool; specify scope of automated vs. confirm-with-human actions (e.g., circuit-breaker activation is 🟢; SLO redefinition is 🟡).
- Draft SKILL.md for ml-evaluation-elevated-standards encoding the 6-stage protocol + non-negotiable rigor checklist from §4.2 and §10.2.
- Draft SKILL.md for ml-incident-response encoding SOP-3 (TTD<15m, TTR<2h, 30-min cadence, escalation triggers).
- Draft SKILL.md for ml-symphony-governance encoding 3-tier autonomy, deployment manifest contents, calibrated uncertainty, L1–L5 maturity.
- Draft template generators (model card, experiment report, architecture comparison, weekly digest, deployment manifest) emitting to Confluence/Slack.
- Cross-check final proposals against subtask 1's coverage matrix; remove anything already covered; ensure no overlap with subtask 2's build-side scope.
</UserRequest>

