## Original User Request
**Description**: Create skills and tools that enable the AI MLE to perform the BUILD-SIDE of the ML lifecycle: training, experiment tracking, hyperparameter optimization, model packaging, registration, feature engineering & data-quality audits, and deployment/rollout. This cluster shares ML Platform auth (Databricks, ML Studio, ML Fabric, Tarot v3, TEAMServe, SageMaker, Tecton/MLFS, Unity Catalog) and is exercised end-to-end by SOP-1 (Drift-Triggered Retraining) and SOP-2 (New Experiment Cycle) and by Day-1 Task #1 (reproduce production model end-to-end).

Proposed new tools (state why existing is insufficient — to be validated against subtask 1's map):
- `mlflow_run_manager` — programmatic creation of MLflow runs following the role's standardized convention (run name `Model_<TS>`, flattened param logging, per-segment metric logging, `mlflow.<framework>.log_model`) against the ML Databricks tracking URI [role doc §4.3].
- `ml_studio_training_job` — launch / monitor / cancel scheduled and event-triggered training jobs on ML Studio + ML Fabric; supports parallel launch of 2–4 alternative architectures per SOP-1 step 3 and 5–10 variants per SOP-2 step 5.
- `optimus_prime_hpo` — drive Bayesian hyperparameter sweeps to statistical convergence (not plateau) with sensitivity analysis [§10.2 #1].
- `tarot_v3_registry` — register model artifacts with compliance metadata, env files, input schema, and lineage; retrieve current production model for reproduce-from-registry workflow [§2 #5, §11.3 #1].
- `tecton_mlfs_features` — define / version / read / write features; emit train-serve consistency checks; generate feature coverage / freshness / sparsity reports per connector/region/tenant [§2 #4, §6 SOP-2 step 4, §11.3 #4].
- `teamserve_deploy`, `sagemaker_deploy`, `triton_endpoint` — deploy models via Micros service descriptors using the role's canonical TEAMServe gRPC endpoint pattern `grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443` [§4.3, §5.1].
- `feature_flag_rollout` — gate canary/shadow rollouts and kill-switches; required for SOP-1 step 7 and §5.3 production patterns.
- `launchpad_preprod` — pre-prod validation runs prior to canary.

Proposed new skills:
- `ml-training-pipeline` (SKILL.md) — guidance for SOP-1 + SOP-2 execution using the tools above; encodes parallel-variants, multi-seed, reproducibility, and elevated-standards rigor [§10.2].
- `model-packaging-and-registration` — guidance for MSP SDK packaging, schema declaration, lineage capture, compliance metadata; uses `tarot_v3_registry` and `mlflow_run_manager`.
- `feature-store-operations` — guidance for MLFS/Tecton lifecycle (generated → written → hydrated → logged → joined-with-labels) and proactive data-quality audits.
- `deployment-and-rollout` — guidance for canary/shadow rollouts, deployment manifest authoring, Spinnaker + Bitbucket Pipelines + Micros workflows, rollback-plan generation.

Research requirement: investigate existing Atlassian-internal MLflow wrappers, ML Studio CLI/SDK, Tarot v3 client, TEAMServe deploy tooling, MSP SDK, Spinnaker/Micros CLIs, Tecton/MLFS SDKs, Launchpad, Optimus Prime; evaluate whether thin wrappers or full new tools are needed. Examine `responsible-ai-api` codebase (role doc §5.3) as the reference for production patterns to encode.

**Todos**:
- Research existing Atlassian-internal SDKs/CLIs for MLflow, ML Studio, ML Fabric, Tarot v3, MSP SDK, TEAMServe, SageMaker, Triton, Tecton/MLFS, Unity Catalog, Spinnaker, Micros, Feature Flags, Launchpad, Optimus Prime; document whether each warrants a thin wrapper tool or a full new implementation.
- For each proposed tool, draft tool.json scope: inputs, outputs, auth model, idempotency, error-handling; ensure parallel-launch support for SOP-1/SOP-2.
- For each proposed skill, draft SKILL.md outline covering when-to-use, tools-it-orchestrates, and elevated-standards checklist (multi-seed, full k-fold, slice-everything, reproducibility).
- Encode feature-store data-quality audit query patterns (coverage / freshness / sparsity per connector/region/tenant) from role doc §6 SOP-2 step 4 and §11.3 task 4.
- Inspect `responsible-ai-api` patterns (two-stage moderation, fail-open kill-switch, per-tenant token bucket, canary auto-rollback) and ensure deployment skill encodes them.
- Cross-check final proposals against subtask 1's coverage matrix; remove anything already covered.
</UserRequest>

