atch/Bootstrap/Execute/Supervise/Close/Learn), policy pack + audit log sink, reasoning-trace persistence, and out-of-band GPU/compute credential provisioning.\n\n**Concerns / notes for downstream subtasks:**\n1. The available toolset is **strong on the Atlassian SDLC + cross-product context layer** but **completely silent on the ML platform plane** — the AI MLE cannot perform any of its core build-side responsibilities (training, registry, serving, feature store, eval) without subtask-2 deliverables.\n2. `bitbucket` already covers PR/Pipeline/repo content workflows — the build-side subtask should treat Spinnaker/Micros as thin wrappers on top, not full reimplementations.\n3. `switcheroo` already provides the feature-flag primitive — subtask 3\'s circuit-breaker skill should *orchestrate* switcheroo, not duplicate it.\n4. `teamwork_graph` + `rovodev` together cover most "instant cross-experiment correlation" needs (§10.4) — subtask 3\'s incident-response skill should compose them rather than build new graph queries.\n5. `socrates` directly enables proactive data-quality audits — subtask 2 should ship reusable SQL templates rather than a new tool surface.\n</Response>', raw_output='Working in \n/Users/tchen7/MyProjects/CoreProjects/OpenStartup/_runtime/tasks/role_setup/role\n_setup_20260524_072327_912f6586\nJira projects: https://hello.atlassian.net/browse/CTSC\n\n\x1b[?2004hCreating agent...\nINTERNAL USE: Your prompts will be recorded to help us improve answer quality. \nTurn off prompt collection with the logging.enablePromptCollection flag in the \nconfig file.\n\n✔ Using model: anthropic:claude-opus-4-7\n✔ Started 23 MCP servers\n\n─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nI\'ll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the role document,\nthen inventory available skills/tools.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  ⬢ Called bash: \n      • _intent: "List workspace and 