ILL step 6 ✓ |\n| 7. Promote winner via flag/canary | `feature_flag_rollout` + `teamserve_deploy.deploy_to_env(canary)`; `deployment-and-rollout` SKILL ✓ |\n\n### SOP-2 (New Experiment Cycle)\n\n| Step | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Hypothesis pinned | `mlflow_run_manager.create_run(tags=...)`; SKILL step 1 ✓ |\n| 2. Feature audit | `tecton_mlfs_features.audit_data_quality`; SKILL step 2 ✓ |\n| 3. Search-space build | Skill step 3 (manual; design discipline) ✓ |\n| 4. DQ gate (§11.3 #4 audit per connector/region/tenant) | `tecton_mlfs_features.audit_data_quality` + **SQL templates embedded in feature-store-operations SKILL** ✓ |\n| 5. Sweep 5-10 parallel variants | `optimus_prime_hpo.create_study(max_parallel=10)` ✓ |\n| 6. Validate in Launchpad | `launchpad_preprod.create_launch` ✓ |\n| 7. Sensitivity analysis | `optimus_prime_hpo.sensitivity_analysis` + §10.2 checklist ✓ |\n| 8. Register winner | `tarot_v3_registry.register_model` ✓ |\n\n### §10.2 Elevated Standards (every item)\n\n| Item | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| HPO to statistical convergence (not plateau) | `optimus_prime_hpo.convergence_policy.require_statistical_convergence=true` ✓ |\n| Full k-fold (≥5) | `ml-training-pipeline` checklist ✓ |\n| Multi-seed (≥5) | `ml-training-pipeline` checklist ✓ |\n| Slice-everything eval | `mlflow_run_manager.log_metrics(segment)` + checklist ✓ |\n| Sensitivity analysis | `optimus_prime_hpo.sensitivity_analysis` ✓ |\n| Reproducibility pinning (SHA, env, snapshot, RNG) | `tarot_v3_registry.register_model` mandatory fields + reproduce_check ✓ |\n\n### Day-1 Task #1 (Reproduce production model end-to-end)\n\n| Step | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Walk back lineage | `tarot_v3_registry.get_lineage` ✓ |\n| 2. Re-pull features at as_of | `tecton_mlfs_features.read_features_for_training(as_of)` ✓ |\n| 3. Re-run training at pinned SHA | `ml_studio_training_job.submit(workflow_ref=…@<sha>)` ✓ |\n| 4. Verify match | `tarot_v3_registry.reproduce_check` (score ≥ 0.99) ✓ |\n| All-in-one acceptance | `model-packaging-and-registration` SKILL "Reproduce-from-Registry" section ✓ |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Shared ML Platform auth — consistency verification\n\nThe breakdown demanded that shared auth (Databricks, ML Studio, ML Fabric, Tarot v3, TEAMServe, SageMaker, Tecton/MLFS, Unity Catalog) be consistently handled. Verification:\n\n| Platform | Credential | Mint pattern | Where defined |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Databricks | `DATABRICKS_TOKEN` (PAT, SSAM-rotated) | direct | `_shared_envelope#/shared_auth/credentials/databricks_token` |\n| ML Studio / ML Fabric | `asap_jwt(aud=ml-studio)` | mint per-call | shared envelope |\n| Tarot v3 | `asap_jwt(aud=tarot-v3)` | mint per-call | shared envelope |\n| TEAMServe (per region/env) | `asap_jwt(aud=teamserve-{region}-{env})` | mint per-call | shared envelope + `teamserve_deploy` |\n| SageMaker | AWS STS via `sagemaker_role_arn` | AssumeRole | shared envelope + `sagemaker_deploy` |\n| Tecton | `TECTON_API_KEY` | direct (when `backend=tecton`) | shared envelope + `tecton_mlfs_features` |\n| MLFS | `asap_jwt(aud=mlfs)` | mint per-call | shared envelope + `tecton_mlfs_features` |\n| Unity Catalog | `asap_jwt(aud=unity-catalog)` | mint per-call | shared envelope + `tecton_mlfs_features` |\n| Optimus Prime | `asap_jwt(aud=optimus-prime)` **EXPERIMENTAL** | mint per-call | shared envelope + tool flagged |\n| Launchpad | `asap_jwt(aud=launchpad)` **EXPERIMENTAL** | mint per-call | shared envelope + tool flagged |\n\n**Result**: All 8 platforms named in the breakdown are present in the shared envelope and every tool that needs them references the cascade via `$ref: _shared_envelope.json#/shared_auth`. Two audiences (`optimus-prime`, `launchpad`) are marked EXPERIMENTAL pending out-of-band confirmation — flagged in §6 below.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Encoded patterns (per breakdown requirement)\n\n### Feature-store DQ audit query templates (§6 SOP-2 step 4, §11.3 #4)\n\nEmbedded verbatim in `feature-store-operations/SKILL.md`:\n1. **Coverage** — non-null rate per slice with `HAVING < {coverage_min}` (default 0.95).\n2. **Freshness** — staleness minutes per slice with `HAVING > {freshness_max_minutes}` (default 60).\n3. **Sparsity** — zero/empty rate per slice with `HAVING > {sparsity_max}` (default 0.30).\n4. **Cardinality drift** — DoD distinct-count delta with `> 20%` threshold.\n5. **Train-serve PSI** — offline vs online distribution divergence with `> 0.10` threshold.\n\nAll five are parameterised and dispatched via `tecton_mlfs_features.audit_data_quality(slice_dimensions=[\'connector\',\'region\',\'tenant_id\'])`.\n\n### Responsible-AI-API production-pattern checklist (§5.3)\n\nEmbedded verbatim in `deployment-and-rollout/SKILL.md` as a 4-pattern mandatory checklist:\n1. **Two-stage moderation** — cascade architecture (Stage 1 fast/recall, Stage 2 slow/precision).\n2. **Fail-open kill-switch** — centralised fail-open path, gated, metric-instrumented.\n3. **Per-tenant token bucket** — keyed on tenant_id, returns 429 + Retry-After.\n4. **Canary auto-rollback** — Spinnaker Safe Release + Kayenta/SignalFx + AZ-balanced + safe-rollback wrapper.\n\nEvery deployment refuses to proceed unless all four boxes are checked.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Gaps & open issues flagged to user\n\n1. **`responsible-ai-api` source tree not in local workspace** (worker_5 flagged) — pattern guidance is derived from role doc narrative + worker_4\'s repo inspection (which DID find the artefacts at `/Users/tchen7/MyProjects/atlassian_packages/responsible-ai-api` or `rai_hack`). Coverage from worker_4 + worker_10 is sufficient; flagged for awareness.\n2. **EXPERIMENTAL slauth audiences**: `optimus-prime`, `launchpad`, possibly `mlfs` and `tarot-v3`. Confirm out-of-band before GA implementation.\n3. **`update_rollout_percentage` capability in Switcheroo MCP**: TBD. If confirmed missing, ship the `feature_flag_rollout` composed wrapper as a tool; otherwise SKILL-only orchestration suffices.\n4. **Tool naming alias**: `tarot_v3_registry` vs `ml_registry_v3` — kept as alias; recommend final name decision from role-doc owner.\n5. **Region/env enumeration is closed** in `teamserve_deploy` — no GCP regions exist in current MSP descriptors. Update enum when GCP is onboarded.\n6. **Optimus Prime vs Praxis-ML HPO vs raw Optuna** — worker_5 noted the role doc doesn\'t name "Optimus Prime" explicitly; the tool is designed platform-agnostic and can re-target.\n7. **Day-1 Task #1 acceptance threshold** — `reproducibility_score ≥ 0.99` is a default; confirm with role-doc owner if a tighter threshold is required for compliance-sensitive models.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Validation & "testing" performed (this aggregation has no executable tests; validation is structural)\n\n| Validation | Method | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| All 8 surviving tools have a tool.json | Directory listing | 8/8 + 1 composed wrapper = 9 files ✓ |\n| All 4 skills have a SKILL.md | Directory listing | 4/4 ✓ |\n| Every tool inherits the shared envelope | grep `$inherits` in `tools/*.json` | 9/9 ✓ |\n| Every SOP-1 step has at least one tool op or skill section | Manual matrix (§3) | 7/7 ✓ |\n| Every SOP-2 step has at least one tool op or skill section | Manual matrix (§3) | 8/8 ✓ |\n| Every §10.2 elevated-standards item covered | Manual matrix (§3) | 6/6 ✓ |\n| Day-1 Task #1 reproduce-from-registry covered end-to-end | Manual matrix + SKILL section | 4/4 steps ✓ |\n| All 8 platform auths consistent | Cross-ref shared envelope (§4) | 8/8 ✓ + 2 EXPERIMENTAL flagged |\n| 5 DQ SQL templates encoded | Manual SKILL inspection | 5/5 ✓ |\n| 4 RAI patterns encoded | Manual SKILL inspection | 4/4 ✓ |\n\n**Summary**: 11 structural validations, 11 pass (with 2 EXPERIMENTAL audience flags surfaced for follow-up).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Composition signatures (for downstream skill orchestrators)\n\n```text\nSOP-1: tecton_mlfs_features.audit_data_quality\n     → tarot_v3_registry.get_lineage\n     → mlflow_run_manager.create_run(parent)\n     → ml_studio_training_job.batch