ore ≥ 0.99` threshold for Day-1 Task #1.\n5. If GCP regions onboard, extend `teamserve_deploy.region` enum.\n6. Implement the 8 standalone tools using the inherited envelope; start with `mlflow_run_manager` (smallest) to validate the envelope contract end-to-end before the larger `teamserve_deploy`.\n', TerminalInferencerResponse(output='The JSON is valid with 5 skills, 18 tools, and 34 gaps mapped. This matches the available skill/MCP toolset inventory I have access to (twg, confluence, jira, research, full-context-mode skills; atlassian, bitbucket, slack, teamwork_graph, compass, atlassian_project/goal/team/tenant, rovodev, socrates, switcheroo, tap, feedback, loom, google_drive, gmail, google_calendar tools — plus the omitted irrelevant ones like s360, gcp, atlassian_tenant being included as low-relevance).\n\nThe file is in place at the required path. Note the task said "Do NOT write any additional files... Only `outputs/role_tool_association.json` should be written" — which I\'ve satisfied.\n\n<Response>\nMapped the AI Machine Learning Engineer role to the agent platform\'s existing inventory and wrote the deliverable to `outputs/role_tool_association.json`.\n\n**Coverage summary:**\n- **5 skills** mapped (high-relevance: `twg`, `confluence`, `jira`; medium: `research`, `full-context-mode`). All five are generic Atlassian/research skills — none are ML-domain skills.\n- **18 MCP toolsets** mapped. High-relevance: `atlassian`, `bitbucket`, `slack`, `teamwork_graph`, `compass`, `rovodev`, `socrates`, `switcheroo`. Medium: `atlassian_project/goal/team`, `tap`, `feedback`. Low: `atlassian_tenant`, `loom`, `google_drive`, `gmail`, `google_calendar`. Omitted as irrelevant: `s360`, `gcp` (sales / translation).\n- Each entry cites specific role-doc sections (§2/§3/§4/§5/§6 SOPs/§7/§8/§10/§11) and includes usage notes derived from inspecting tool schemas, not names alone.\n\n**Key coverage strengths (full):**\n- Stakeholder communication, runbook/PIR/model-card publishin